window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-kushida-kikyou"]=[{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p19-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo entrance ceremony bus  the public champion crowded city bus heading to anhs on entrance ceremony morning  an elderly woman is standing in the aisle  unsteady on her feet  an office lady scolds koenji first  most passengers look away or pretend not to notice  an unnamed girl wearing the anhs uniform   the text never names her here  but she is the one later understood to be kushida  see  note    steps forward from the aisle and directly faces koenji  who is lounging in the priority seating   um  i think that the lady is right   unexpected support  delivered brave and frank   this poor woman appears to have been suffering for quite some time now  won t you offer up your seat  while you might consider such courtesy unnecessary  i think it would contribute greatly to society  when koenji haughtily refuses and declares he cares only for his own satisfaction  she refuses to back down or accept defeat  instead of retreating  she turns to face the entire crowded bus without fear   everyone  please listen to me for just a moment  won t someone give up their seat for this woman  it doesn t matter who  please  extraordinary social courage and charisma  her appeal moves an office lady to stand and surrender her seat out of guilt  e excuse me  you can have mine  settling the matter  earnest  pleading  gentle  highly moral public register that commands collective attention without sounding aggressive  direct moral clash  attempts to appeal to social conscience against his absolute solipsism  the bus text never names the uniformed challenger  her identification with kushida is an inference  she later knows ak and horikita spoke at the gate that day  p 57  not a stated fact in year 1  vol  1","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Entrance ceremony bus: the public champion<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.19–24<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Crowded city bus heading to ANHS on entrance ceremony morning. An elderly woman is standing in the aisle, unsteady on her feet. An office lady scolds Kōenji first; most passengers look away or pretend not to notice.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Um… I think that the lady is right.” (unexpected support, delivered brave and frank)<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“This poor woman appears to have been suffering for quite some time now. Won’t you offer up your seat? While you might consider such courtesy unnecessary, I think it would contribute greatly to society.”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Everyone, please listen to me for just a moment. Won’t someone give up their seat for this woman? It doesn’t matter who. Please.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> An unnamed girl wearing the ANHS uniform — the text never names her here, but she is the one later understood to be Kushida (see [note]) — steps forward from the aisle and directly faces Kōenji, who is lounging in the priority seating.<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Kōenji haughtily refuses and declares he cares only for his own satisfaction, she refuses to back down or accept defeat. Instead of retreating, she turns to face the entire crowded bus without fear.<span class=\"pg\">p.21–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Extraordinary social courage and charisma; her appeal moves an office lady to stand and surrender her seat out of guilt (“E-excuse me. You can have mine.”), settling the matter.<span class=\"pg\">p.22–24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Earnest, pleading, gentle, highly moral public register that commands collective attention without sounding aggressive.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Direct moral clash; attempts to appeal to social conscience against his absolute solipsism.<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The bus text never names the uniformed challenger. Her identification with Kushida is an inference (she later knows AK and Horikita spoke at the gate that day, p.57), not a stated fact in Year 1, Vol. 1.<span class=\"pg\">p.19–24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p34-1\">→ After: Classroom Day 1: empathetic rescue &amp; friendship declaration<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p34-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo classroom day 1  empathetic rescue   friendship declaration established as the idol and social anchor of class 1 d  class 1 d classroom after homeroom orientation  hirata asks students to introduce themselves from the front row  inogashira kokoro freezes at her desk  trembling and pale  classmates mistakenly shout  do your best  which heightens her panic  kushida steps in with immediate  emotionally intelligent guidance   it s okay to go slowly  don t rush  instinctive social psychology  understands that  do your best  applies forceful pressure  whereas  just take things slowly  don t rush  removes urgency and restores calm  inogashira successfully finishes her intro  steps up cheerfully as the next speaker  glowing with approachable energy   my name is kushida kikyou  none of my friends from junior high made it to this school  so i m alone here  i d like to get to know all of your names and faces right away and become friends as soon as possible   my first goal is to become friends with everyone  so  after we re finished with introductions  i d love for you to share your contact information with me   so  after school or during vacations  i want to make all sorts of memories with lots of people  please feel free to invite me to lots and lots of events  anyway  i ve talked for a long time  so i ll end my introduction here  outward persona  boundless warmth  radical accessibility  open hearted desire to unite the entire class and befriend every student without distinction  instantly established as the undisputed idol and social anchor of class 1 d","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p34-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Classroom Day 1: empathetic rescue &amp; friendship declaration<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.34–35<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom after homeroom orientation. Hirata asks students to introduce themselves from the front row.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s okay to go slowly. Don’t rush.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“My name is Kushida Kikyou. None of my friends from junior high made it to this school, so I’m alone here. I’d like to get to know all of your names and faces right away and become friends as soon as possible!”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“My first goal is to become friends with everyone. So, after we’re finished with introductions, I’d love for you to share your contact information with me!”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Established as the idol and social anchor of Class 1-D.<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Inogashira Kokoro freezes at her desk, trembling and pale. Classmates mistakenly shout “Do your best!” which heightens her panic. Kushida steps in with immediate, emotionally intelligent guidance.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Instinctive social psychology: understands that “Do your best!” applies forceful pressure, whereas “Just take things slowly. Don’t rush,” removes urgency and restores calm. Inogashira successfully finishes her intro.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Steps up cheerfully as the next speaker, glowing with approachable energy.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, after school or during vacations, I want to make all sorts of memories with lots of people. Please feel free to invite me to lots and lots of events! Anyway, I’ve talked for a long time, so I’ll end my introduction here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Outward persona: boundless warmth, radical accessibility, open-hearted desire to unite the entire class and befriend every student without distinction.<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Instantly established as the undisputed idol and social anchor of Class 1-D.<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p19-1\">← Before: Entrance ceremony bus: the public champion<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p56-1\">→ After: Corridor interception: probing for Horikita&#x27;s secrets<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p56-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo corridor interception  probing for horikita s secrets on ayanokoji s way out of the classroom at lunch on day 2  he d resolved to eat alone  kushida approaches him with a radiant smile  holding something he can t identify   possibly a pouch covered in key holders  calls out to him cheerfully  you re ayanokouji kun  right  ayanokoji s heart pounds like a jackhammer at her beauty  short  straight dyed brown hair  one of the newly approved short skirt lengths   i m kushida  from your class  do you remember me  she asked   to tell you the truth  there s something i wanted to ask you  it s just one little question  ayanokouji kun  are you on good terms with horikita san   oh  no  well  do you remember when i said i wanted to get along with everyone in class  that s why i wanted everyone s contact info  but  horikita turned me down  when he says he barely knows horikita  she pivots to probing what kind of person she is  then frames her interest as pointed  worry   i was just wondering what kind of person horikita san is   kushida continued   is she the type who ll talk a lot when she s with a friend   well  during our introductions  horikita san walked out of the classroom  right  it seems like she hasn t talked to anybody yet  so i m a little worried about her   hmm  i see  i thought that you two must have been old friends before starting school here  i m sorry to have asked you such a strange question   how  you introduced yourself the other day  didn t you  i remembered   she d listened to his hopelessly lame self introduction  closes with a radiant handshake   well  it s nice to meet you again  ayanokouji kun  relentless social campaigner  frames investigative probing as friendly concern  remembers even the least remarkable classmates  introductions  warmth weaponized as an information gathering tool  bubbly  innocent  persistently encouraging  masking an unyielding determination  fixation begins  determined to break through horikita s barriers  encodes her as the girl who refused contact info and  hasn t talked to anybody yet  recruits him as her bridge and information source to reach horikita  establishes their first warm real world contact  handshake","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p56-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Corridor interception: probing for Horikita&#x27;s secrets<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.56–57<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On Ayanokōji’s way out of the classroom at lunch on Day 2 (he’d resolved to eat alone). Kushida approaches him with a radiant smile, holding something he can’t identify — possibly a pouch covered in key holders.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m Kushida, from your class. Do you remember me?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“To tell you the truth, there’s something I wanted to ask you. It’s just one little question. Ayanokouji-kun, are you on good terms with Horikita-san?”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh, no. Well, do you remember when I said I wanted to get along with everyone in class? That’s why I wanted everyone’s contact info. But… Horikita turned me down.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Calls out to him cheerfully (“You’re Ayanokouji-kun, right?”); Ayanokōji’s heart pounds like a jackhammer at her beauty (short, straight dyed-brown hair, one of the newly approved short skirt lengths).<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When he says he barely knows Horikita, she pivots to probing what kind of person she is, then frames her interest as pointed “worry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was just wondering what kind of person Horikita-san is,” (Kushida continued)<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is she the type who’ll talk a lot when she’s with a friend?”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, during our introductions, Horikita-san walked out of the classroom, right? It seems like she hasn’t talked to anybody yet, so I’m a little worried about her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm. I see. I thought that you two must have been old friends before starting school here. I’m sorry to have asked you such a strange question.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How? You introduced yourself the other day, didn’t you? I remembered.” (she’d listened to his hopelessly lame self-introduction)<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Closes with a radiant handshake: “Well, it’s nice to meet you again, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Relentless social campaigner; frames investigative probing as friendly concern; remembers even the least remarkable classmates’ introductions; warmth weaponized as an information-gathering tool.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Bubbly, innocent, persistently encouraging, masking an unyielding determination.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Fixation begins: determined to break through Horikita’s barriers; encodes her as the girl who refused contact info and “hasn’t talked to anybody yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Recruits him as her bridge and information source to reach Horikita; establishes their first warm real-world contact (handshake).<span class=\"pg\">p.56–57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p34-1\">← Before: Classroom Day 1: empathetic rescue &amp; friendship declaration<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p79-1\">→ After: Swim heat &amp; detecting Ayanokōji&#x27;s physique<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p79-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo swim heat   detecting ayanokoji s physique indoor swimming pool  races in the second girls  swimming heat  claims she wasn t good at swimming in junior high  yet finishes second with a very respectable time of  approximately 31 seconds  stands beside ayanokoji by the pool deck in her school swimsuit  watches koenji and sudo with genuine enthusiasm   i m really looking forward to this  both kouejin kun and sudou kun are so fast   corpus renders koenji s name as  kouejin kun  here   kept verbatim   hmm  what s the matter  your face looks red for some reason  are you not feeling well  by chance   you re much faster than average  too  ayanokouji kun  observes ayanokoji s bare upper body with keen perception  looking at his muscular build with shock and awe   is that so  but you look like a really manly guy  ayanokouji kun  even though you re so slim  i could say that you re even better built than sudou  and he plays basketball  perceptive observation  first classmate to pierce ayanokoji s unassuming exterior and physically recognize his elite  hidden muscle development despite his deflections about  good genes  casual  warm banter  notices his flushed nervousness and compliments his physique","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p79-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Swim heat &amp; detecting Ayanokōji&#x27;s physique<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.79, 87–88<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Indoor swimming pool.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m really looking forward to this. Both Kouejin-kun and Sudou-kun are so fast,” (corpus renders Kōenji’s name as “Kouejin-kun” here — kept verbatim)<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hmm? What’s the matter? Your face looks red for some reason. Are you not feeling well, by chance?”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re much faster than average, too, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Races in the second girls&#x27; swimming heat; claims she wasn&#x27;t good at swimming in junior high, yet finishes second with a very respectable time of **approximately 31 seconds**.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands beside Ayanokōji by the pool deck in her school swimsuit; watches Kōenji and Sudō with genuine enthusiasm.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Observes Ayanokōji&#x27;s bare upper body with keen perception, looking at his muscular build with shock and awe.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that so? But you look like a really manly guy, Ayanokouji-kun. Even though you’re so slim, I could say that you’re even better built than Sudou, and he plays basketball.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Perceptive observation: first classmate to pierce Ayanokōji&#x27;s unassuming exterior and physically recognize his elite, hidden muscle development despite his deflections about &quot;good genes&quot;.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Casual, warm banter; notices his flushed nervousness and compliments his physique.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p56-1\">← Before: Corridor interception: probing for Horikita&#x27;s secrets<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p89-1\">→ After: Café trap failure &amp; the compulsion for 100% friendship<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p89-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo cafe trap failure   the compulsion for 100  friendship classroom 1 d  outside dorms  then palate cafe in keyaki mall  smilingly invites horikita to a cafe after class  when told not to invite her again because it s a bother  kushida maintains her bright grin and promises   i ll invite you again  waits outside the dormitory for ayanokoji  takes his hand warmly  stepping into his personal space with a floral scent   i ll just ask you outright  ayanokouji kun  have you seen horikita san smile even once  conspires with ayanokoji to stage an ambush meeting disguised as coincidence at palate cafe in keyaki mall  directing him to lure horikita there under the pretense of treating her to tea  palate cafe  kushida walks in  acting surprised  but horikita immediately exposes the four person table and nervous glances as a transparent setup  faced with horikita s icy refusal to sit  kushida mumbles an ominous hint of prior recognition   horikita san  whatever you say  i really want to be friends with you  when i saw you  i felt like it wasn t the first time we d met  i wondered if you felt the same way  horikita cuts her off  drops her bombshell about being alone for nine consecutive years  and leaves  kushida collapses silently into her seat  genuinely stunned and winded by the brutal rebuff  recovers her trademark sunshine smile in a split second   it s okay  thank you  ayanokouji kun  it s true that i wasn t able to become her friend  but i was able to learn something important  that s enough for me  moves to sit beside ayanokoji at the table  when asked why she is so desperate to befriend horikita when she already has more friends than anyone else  kushida reveals her underlying psychological compulsion   i wanted to be friends with everyone  not just the people in class d  but the students from other classes  too  but if i can t become friends with one girl in my class  then that means i ll never achieve my goal  terrifying emotional switch  can collapse in despair and snap back to a beaming smile in an instant  driven by an absolute  obsessive psychological need for 100  universal social acceptance a single holdout  horikita  invalidates her entire self worth  suspects or hints at a prior encounter from junior high  fixated on conquering her wall  deepens alliance  relies on him as a co conspirator  surprised to learn he was also friendless in junior high","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p89-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Café trap failure &amp; the compulsion for 100% friendship<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.89, 91–93, 98–101<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D; outside dorms; then Palate Café in Keyaki Mall. Palate Café. Kushida walks in, acting surprised, but Horikita immediately exposes the four-person table and nervous glances as a transparent setup.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll just ask you outright. Ayanokouji-kun, have you seen Horikita-san smile even once?”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Horikita-san, whatever you say, I really want to be friends with you. When I saw you, I felt like it wasn’t the first time we’d met. I wondered if you felt the same way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s okay. Thank you, Ayanokouji-kun. It’s true that I wasn’t able to become her friend, but…I was able to learn something important. That’s enough for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Smilingly invites Horikita to a café after class; when told not to invite her again because it&#x27;s a bother, Kushida maintains her bright grin and promises: *“I’ll invite you again.”*<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Waits outside the dormitory for Ayanokōji. Takes his hand warmly, stepping into his personal space with a floral scent.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Conspires with Ayanokōji to stage an ambush meeting disguised as coincidence at Palate Café in Keyaki Mall, directing him to lure Horikita there under the pretense of treating her to tea.<span class=\"pg\">p.91–93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Faced with Horikita&#x27;s icy refusal to sit, Kushida mumbles an ominous hint of prior recognition.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Horikita cuts her off, drops her bombshell about being alone for nine consecutive years, and leaves.<span class=\"pg\">p.99–100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Kushida collapses silently into her seat, genuinely stunned and winded by the brutal rebuff.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Recovers her trademark sunshine smile in a split-second.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Moves to sit beside Ayanokōji at the table. When asked why she is so desperate to befriend Horikita when she already has more friends than anyone else, Kushida reveals her underlying psychological compulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wanted to be friends with everyone. Not just the people in Class D, but the students from other classes, too. But if I can’t become friends with one girl in my class, then that means I’ll never achieve my goal…”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Terrifying emotional switch: can collapse in despair and snap back to a beaming smile in an instant; driven by an absolute, obsessive psychological need for 100% universal social acceptance—a single holdout (Horikita) invalidates her entire self-worth.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Suspects or hints at a prior encounter from junior high; fixated on conquering her wall.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Deepens alliance; relies on him as a co-conspirator; surprised to learn he was also friendless in junior high.<span class=\"pg\">p.91, 100–101<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p79-1\">← Before: Swim heat &amp; detecting Ayanokōji&#x27;s physique<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p117-1\">→ After: Group outing &amp; grounding Yamauchi<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p117-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo group outing   grounding yamauchi keyaki mall boutique and cafe  participates in the class shopping outing with hirata  karuizawa  ike  yamauchi  and ayanokoji   ha ha  i get the feeling ike kun is enjoying his time here to the fullest   do you mean you ll lose your sense of money management  yeah  that does sound pretty scary  actually   concurs with hirata that unearned wealth is dangerous   what about you  ayanokouji kun  do you think that 100 000 points is a lot or not enough  when yamauchi absurdly boasts that he scored 900 points on the  apec  kushida gently and politely brings him back to reality without embarrassing him   um  don t you mean the toeic  not apec  socially unifying  attentive to everyone in the conversation  checks in on quiet members  ayanokoji  defuses male boasting with gentle charm","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Group outing &amp; grounding Yamauchi<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.117–118<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Keyaki Mall boutique and café.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ha ha! I get the feeling Ike-kun is enjoying his time here to the fullest!”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do you mean you’ll lose your sense of money management? Yeah, that does sound pretty scary, actually.” (concurs with Hirata that unearned wealth is dangerous).<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What about you, Ayanokouji-kun? Do you think that 100,000 points is a lot or not enough?”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Participates in the class shopping outing with Hirata, Karuizawa, Ike, Yamauchi, and Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Yamauchi absurdly boasts that he scored 900 points on the &quot;APEC&quot;, Kushida gently and politely brings him back to reality without embarrassing him.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Um, don’t you mean the TOEIC, not APEC?”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Socially unifying, attentive to everyone in the conversation, checks in on quiet members (Ayanokōji), defuses male boasting with gentle charm.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p89-1\">← Before: Café trap failure &amp; the compulsion for 100% friendship<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p131-1\">→ After: De-escalating violence &amp; lending points without hesitation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p131-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo de escalating violence   lending points without hesitation classroom 1 d  may 1st panic and lunch break  steps fearlessly between yukimura and hirata as yukimura grabs hirata s collar  gently envelops yukimura s clenched fist with both hands to disarm his fury   calm down  you two  okay  i m sure that the teacher talked to us harshly so we d be inspired to do better  right  besides  it s only been one month since we started here  right  like hirata kun said  it s better if we all do our best together  do you think that i m wrong about that  supreme emotional de escalation  completely diffuses a physical altercation within seconds using gentle physical contact and moral appeal  verbally supports hirata s appeal from the podium when sudo pushes back against rules   well  the teacher did say that the being late and talking in class were obviously bad  right  when karuizawa casually hits her up for 2 000 private points to cover her deficit  kushida agrees immediately without a shred of reluctance   okay  sure  explains her philosophy to ayanokoji when he warns that she will likely never see those points returned   i can t just ignore a friend in need  karuizawa san has a lot of friends  too  so i think it s probably hard for her not to have any points   wait  how do you transfer points   this school really does take great care of its students  it even has a way to help students like karuizawa san  alerts ayanokoji when the school pa summons him to the faculty office   looks like the teacher wants to see you  pathological altruism   selfless facade  parts with her personal financial safety net instantly to preserve social harmony and project the perfect  supportive classmate persona  acts as an unconditional financial and emotional safety valve  integral co mediator  provides the emotional anchor that backs up his structural leadership","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p131-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">De-escalating violence &amp; lending points without hesitation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.131–132, 134, 138–139<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D, May 1st panic and lunch break.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Calm down, you two, okay? I’m sure that the teacher talked to us harshly so we’d be inspired to do better, right?… Besides, it’s only been one month since we started here, right? Like Hirata-kun said, it’s better if we all do…”<span class=\"pg\">p.131–132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, the teacher did say that the being late and talking in class were obviously bad, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Okay, sure.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Steps fearlessly between Yukimura and Hirata as Yukimura grabs Hirata&#x27;s collar; gently envelops Yukimura’s clenched fist with both hands to disarm his fury.<span class=\"pg\">p.131–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Calm down, you two, okay? I’m sure that the teacher talked to us harshly so we’d be inspired to do better, right?… Besides, it’s only been one month since we started here, right? Like Hirata-kun said, it’s better if we all do our best together. Do you think that I’m wrong about that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.131–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Supreme emotional de-escalation: completely diffuses a physical altercation within seconds using gentle physical contact and moral appeal.<span class=\"pg\">p.131–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Verbally supports Hirata’s appeal from the podium when Sudō pushes back against rules.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Karuizawa casually hits her up for 2,000 private points to cover her deficit, Kushida agrees immediately without a shred of reluctance.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Explains her philosophy to Ayanokōji when he warns that she will likely never see those points returned.<span class=\"pg\">p.138–139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t just ignore a friend in need. Karuizawa-san has a lot of friends, too, so I think it’s probably hard for her not to have any points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, how do you transfer points?”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This school really does take great care of its students. It even has a way to help students like Karuizawa-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Alerts Ayanokōji when the school PA summons him to the faculty office.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like the teacher wants to see you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Pathological altruism / selfless facade: parts with her personal financial safety net instantly to preserve social harmony and project the perfect, supportive classmate persona.<span class=\"pg\">p.138–139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Acts as an unconditional financial and emotional safety valve.<span class=\"pg\">p.138–139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Integral co-mediator; provides the emotional anchor that backs up his structural leadership.<span class=\"pg\">p.131–132, 134<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p117-1\">← Before: Group outing &amp; grounding Yamauchi<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p162-1\">→ After: Recruiting the failures &amp; library study session<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p162-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo recruiting the failures   library study session hallway outside classroom 1 d  then school library  approached by ayanokoji after school  eagerly agrees to help gather sudo  ike  and yamauchi for horikita s midterm study group   rejoice  kushida  you ve been selected as an ambassador of goodwill  tomorrow  your hard work begins   ak to kushida   well  i do want to get closer to her  but  well  i won t worry about that now  besides  it s only natural to help out a friend in need   it s cruel to expel someone for getting a bad grade  isn t it awful to have to say goodbye after you ve worked to become friends with everyone  i ll do anything i can to be useful  grasps ayanokoji s hand warmly with an irresistible beaming smile  sets her condition  insists that she also be allowed to participate in the study group   ah  but there s just one thing i want to ask you  i want to participate in the study group  too  yes  i want to study with everyone  asks ayanokoji point blank if he and horikita are dating  reporting widespread rumors among the girls that the solitary horikita only opens up to him   this might be too forward  but are you two already dating  it s a big rumor among the girls in our class  you know  they say that even though horikita san is always alone  she only seems to get along really well with you  ayanokouji kun  and you guys eat together  after all  successfully secures ayanokoji s phone number  successfully mobilizes ike  yamauchi  and sudo via text within hours using her feminine charm  arrives at the library wearing casual clothes  sits beside horikita  brings snacks  and tries desperately to soothe the tension between horikita and the failing boys  when horikita declares the failing boys are  dead weight  better off expelled  kushida is deeply distressed   horikita san  we re not going to be able to study with anyone if things continue like this   is it wrong  i don t want to abandon sudou kun  ike kun  and yamauchi kun  hurt and dismayed when horikita accuses her of not genuinely caring about them  leaves the library resolved to find another way to save them   what  i don t understand  why do you say things like that  horikita san  why do you try to antagonize people  that s very sad","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p162-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Recruiting the failures &amp; library study session<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.162–165, 173–175<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hallway outside Classroom 1-D; then school library.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Rejoice, Kushida. You’ve been selected as an ambassador of goodwill. Tomorrow, your hard work begins.” (AK to Kushida)<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, I do want to get closer to her, but… well, I won’t worry about that now. Besides, it’s only natural to help out a friend in need.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s cruel to expel someone for getting a bad grade. Isn’t it awful to have to say goodbye after you’ve worked to become friends with everyone?… I’ll do anything I can to be useful!”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Approached by Ayanokōji after school; eagerly agrees to help gather Sudō, Ike, and Yamauchi for Horikita&#x27;s midterm study group.<span class=\"pg\">p.162–163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Grasps Ayanokōji&#x27;s hand warmly with an irresistible beaming smile.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sets her condition: insists that she also be allowed to participate in the study group.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, but there’s just one thing I want to ask you. I want to participate in the study group, too… Yes. I want to study with everyone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Asks Ayanokōji point-blank if he and Horikita are dating, reporting widespread rumors among the girls that the solitary Horikita only opens up to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This might be too forward, but are you two already dating?… It’s a big rumor among the girls in our class, you know. They say that even though Horikita-san is always alone, she only seems to get along really well with you, Ayanokouji-kun. And you guys eat together, after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Successfully secures Ayanokōji&#x27;s phone number.<span class=\"pg\">p.165–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Successfully mobilizes Ike, Yamauchi, and Sudō via text within hours using her feminine charm.<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Arrives at the library wearing casual clothes; sits beside Horikita, brings snacks, and tries desperately to soothe the tension between Horikita and the failing boys.<span class=\"pg\">p.173–175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Horikita declares the failing boys are &quot;dead weight&quot; better off expelled, Kushida is deeply distressed.<span class=\"pg\">p.178–179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san, we’re not going to be able to study with anyone if things continue like this…”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it wrong? I don’t want to abandon Sudou-kun, Ike-kun, and Yamauchi-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hurt and dismayed when Horikita accuses her of not genuinely caring about them; leaves the library resolved to find another way to save them.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What? I don’t understand. Why do you say things like that, Horikita-san? Why do you try to antagonize people? That’s…very sad.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p131-1\">← Before: De-escalating violence &amp; lending points without hesitation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p181-1\">→ After: Rooftop unmasking &amp; the sexual assault blackmail frame<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p181-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo rooftop unmasking   the sexual assault blackmail frame school rooftop and stairwell landing  dusk  around 6 00 pm  believing herself completely alone on the locked rooftop  drops her sweet  angelic persona entirely  viciously vents raw  murderous hatred toward horikita suzune in a harsh  guttural voice   ahhh  so annoying   she s seriously annoying  god  how irritating  it d be better if she just died   ugh  i hate stuck up  snobby girls who think they re so cute  why is she such a harpy  a rotten girl like her couldn t possibly tutor me   ah  she s the worst  she s just the worst  the worst  the worst  horikita  you re so annoying  you re so damn annoying  hears ayanokoji accidentally kick the rooftop door  instantly freezes  turns  and locks onto him with a chilling  predatory glare   what are you doing here   did you hear  marches down the stairs  places her left forearm against ayanokoji s throat  and pins him hard against the wall  her tone  her actions  everything about her completely unlike the kushida he knew  her expression almost comparable to horikita s   if you tell anyone what you just heard  i won t forgive you   her words were ice   not an idle threat   in that case  i would tell everyone that you raped me  she said   that s okay  it wouldn t be false   her words had heft and power  leaving him unable to reply  grabs his right wrist  slowly opens his hand  and pushes his palm up against her breast  holding it there despite his attempts to pull away   your fingerprints are on my clothes  that s evidence of my claim  i m being serious  understand   i m going to leave this uniform in my room without washing it  if you betray me  i ll hand it over to the police   it s a promise  she said   steps away   that s none of your business   when ak asks which is the real her   is it bad to want everyone to like you  do you understand how difficult it is to accomplish that  you can t know  can you  she asked   at least on the surface  i wanted to appear to get along with horikita   yeah  that s what i want out of life  though  that way  my existence has meaning   answered without hesitation  her internal rules demand she get close to horikita   let me tell you something  while i have the chance  i absolutely despise gloomy  ordinary guys like you   what the  i don t know what you mean  did horikita san say something about me  she snapped   when ak probes whether they knew each other before school   just shut up  hearing you talk irritates me  ayanokouji kun  i only want to know one thing  do you swear you ll never tell anyone what you learned here today   okay  i believe you  ayanokouji kun   closes her eyes and slowly exhales   you know  ayanokouji kun  you re the only one that horikita san opens up to  after extracting his oath  the terrifying mask drops  she pivots smoothly into reflective analysis of horikita as  the complete opposite  of herself  psychopathic dual personality   dark side  underneath the angelic  universally adored school idol lies a vicious  foul mouthed sadist harboring burning hatred for anyone who rejects her  especially horikita  chillingly pragmatic and capable of fabricating sexual assault charges with forensic precision to protect her secret  secret  venomous obsession and hatred  wishes she would die  considers her an unbearable  stuck up harpy  traps him via manufactured sexual assault evidence  fingerprints  unwashed uniform  and an unwinnable credibility contest  extracts a sworn oath  then reverts to warmth  establishes an uneasy  deadly truce","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p181-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Rooftop unmasking &amp; the sexual assault blackmail frame<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.181–186<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">School rooftop and stairwell landing, dusk (around 6:00 PM).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ahhh, so annoying!”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“She’s seriously annoying! God, how irritating. It’d be better if she just died…”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ugh, I hate stuck-up, snobby girls who think they’re so cute. Why is she such a harpy? A rotten girl like her couldn’t possibly tutor me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>26 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Believing herself completely alone on the locked rooftop, drops her sweet, angelic persona entirely. Viciously vents raw, murderous hatred toward Horikita Suzune in a harsh, guttural voice.<span class=\"pg\">p.181–182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, she’s the worst! She’s just the worst, the worst, the worst! Horikita, you’re so annoying! You’re so damn annoying!”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hears Ayanokōji accidentally kick the rooftop door; instantly freezes, turns, and locks onto him with a chilling, predatory glare.<span class=\"pg\">p.182–183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What…are you…doing here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you hear?”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Marches down the stairs, places her left forearm against Ayanokōji’s throat, and pins him hard against the wall; her tone, her actions, everything about her completely unlike the Kushida he knew (her expression almost comparable to Horikita’s).<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you tell anyone what you just heard, I won’t forgive you.” (her words were ice — not an idle threat)<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, I would tell everyone that you raped me,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s okay. It wouldn’t be false.” (her words had heft and power, leaving him unable to reply)<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Grabs his right wrist, slowly opens his hand, and pushes his palm up against her breast, holding it there despite his attempts to pull away.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your fingerprints are on my clothes. That’s evidence of my claim. I’m being serious. Understand?”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m going to leave this uniform in my room without washing it. If you betray me, I’ll hand it over to the police.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s a promise,” she said. (steps away)<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s none of your business.” (when AK asks which is the real her)<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it bad to want everyone to like you? Do you understand how difficult it is to accomplish that? You can’t know, can you?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At least on the surface, I wanted to appear to get along with Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. That’s what I want out of life, though. That way, my existence has meaning.” (answered without hesitation; her internal rules demand she get close to Horikita)<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let me tell you something, while I have the chance. I absolutely despise gloomy, ordinary guys like you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What the… I don’t know what you mean. Did Horikita-san say something about me?” she snapped. (when AK probes whether they knew each other before school)<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just shut up. Hearing you talk irritates me, Ayanokouji-kun. I only want to know one thing. Do you swear you’ll never tell anyone what you learned here today?”<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. I believe you, Ayanokouji-kun.” (closes her eyes and slowly exhales)<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You know, Ayanokouji-kun, you’re the only one that Horikita-san opens up to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After extracting his oath, the terrifying mask drops; she pivots smoothly into reflective analysis of Horikita as “the complete opposite” of herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Psychopathic dual personality / dark side: underneath the angelic, universally adored school idol lies a vicious, foul-mouthed sadist harboring burning hatred for anyone who rejects her (especially Horikita); chillingly pragmatic and capable of fabricating sexual assault charges with forensic precision to protect her secret.<span class=\"pg\">p.181–186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Secret, venomous obsession and hatred; wishes she would die; considers her an unbearable, stuck-up harpy.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Traps him via manufactured sexual-assault evidence (fingerprints, unwashed uniform) and an unwinnable credibility contest; extracts a sworn oath, then reverts to warmth; establishes an uneasy, deadly truce.<span class=\"pg\">p.183–186<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p162-1\">← Before: Recruiting the failures &amp; library study session<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p204-1\">→ After: Class A partnership, the ally test &amp; the secret bond<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p204-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo class a partnership  the ally test   the secret bond accepts horikita s unprecedented lunch invitation at palate  probes her motive  is it really for sudou kun and the others  and is satisfied by the blunt selfish answer   you re free to think whatever you like  i just didn t want you to try to lie to me  i m glad you were honest  okay  i ll help  we re classmates  after all  right  ayanokouji kun   no  not for that  i want to work on getting into class a with you  i want to help with everything else you ll be doing   elevates her ask from study group helper to class a partner   really  yay   cheers  the three of them shake hands   her left and right arms extended to horikita and ak  immediately takes charge of luring the boys back  ike and yamauchi arrive visibly on cloud nine from her invitations  plays along with ayanokoji s boyfriend bait by raising the stakes into a public motive   w well then  how about this  i ll go on a date with whoever scores highest on the test  i like people who work really hard  even when they don t like doing it  waves horikita off from across the room after ambushing ak into a lunch date   possibly engineered  had she planned that  by chance  keeps visible tabs on ayanokoji post rooftop   those girls are just being realists  you can t afford to eat on dreams alone   on the third year girls swarming kouenji   you re ranked a respectable fifth place in the hot guy rankings  congratulations  by the way  satonaka kun in class a is in first place  hirata kun s in second   relays the girls  anonymous ranking charts   talking to you is fun  ayanokouji kun     ha ha ha  yes  i did  hate you  sorry  but that s how i really feel   smiling  unrepentant  reveals the true purpose of the lunch  an alliance stress test between herself and horikita   if horikita and i happen to clash  i hope that you ll cooperate with me  ayanokouji kun   first  we d need to build a relationship of mutual trust   declining to explain her situation until trust is established  accepts ak s errand  broadcast chabashira s revised test material list to all of class d  including hirata s group  co conspirator on the old test operation  agrees to take public credit as the receiver  from a third year student you re close to  so ayanokoji stays invisible   don t you feel that a strange bond of mutual trust forms between people who share a secret  honest about being manipulative mode around ak  alliance ambition  candid roasts  and veiled threats delivered under an unbroken smile  secures conditional partnership with the class a project   her biggest proximity gain to date  explicitly stakes a claim on his loyalty  wraps the old test secret as mutual trust bonding","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p204-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Class A partnership, the ally test &amp; the secret bond<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.204–217, 226, 233–235<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re free to think whatever you like. I just didn’t want you to try to lie to me. I’m glad you were honest. Okay, I’ll help. We’re classmates, after all. Right, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“No, not for that. I want to work on getting into Class A with you. I want to help with everything else you’ll be doing.” (elevates her ask from study-group helper to Class A partner)<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Really?! Yay!” (cheers; the three of them shake hands — her left and right arms extended to Horikita and AK)<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Accepts Horikita&#x27;s unprecedented lunch invitation at Palate; probes her motive (&quot;Is it really for Sudou-kun and the others?&quot;) and is satisfied by the blunt selfish answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Immediately takes charge of luring the boys back; Ike and Yamauchi arrive visibly on cloud nine from her invitations.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Plays along with Ayanokōji&#x27;s boyfriend bait by raising the stakes into a public motive: “W-well then, how about this? I’ll go on a date with whoever scores highest on the test. I like people who work really hard, even when they don’t like doing it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210–211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Waves Horikita off from across the room after ambushing AK into a lunch date — possibly engineered (&quot;Had she planned that, by chance?&quot;); keeps visible tabs on Ayanokōji post-rooftop.<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Those girls are just being realists. You can’t afford to eat on dreams alone.” (on the third-year girls swarming Kouenji)<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re ranked a respectable fifth place in the hot guy rankings. Congratulations! By the way, Satonaka-kun in Class A is in first place. Hirata-kun’s in second.” (relays the girls&#x27; anonymous ranking charts)<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Talking to you is fun, Ayanokouji-kun.” / “Ha ha ha, yes, I did [hate you]. Sorry, but that’s how I really feel.” (smiling, unrepentant)<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Reveals the true purpose of the lunch: an alliance stress-test between herself and Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If Horikita and I happen to clash, I hope that you’ll cooperate with me, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “First, we’d need to build a relationship of mutual trust.” (declining to explain her situation until trust is established)<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Accepts AK&#x27;s errand: broadcast Chabashira&#x27;s revised test-material list to all of Class D, including Hirata&#x27;s group.<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Co-conspirator on the old-test operation; agrees to take public credit as the receiver (&quot;from a third-year student you&#x27;re close to&quot;) so Ayanokōji stays invisible.<span class=\"pg\">p.233–235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you feel that a strange bond of mutual trust forms between people who share a secret?”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Honest-about-being-manipulative mode around AK: alliance ambition, candid roasts, and veiled threats delivered under an unbroken smile.<span class=\"pg\">p.204–217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Secures conditional partnership with the Class A project — her biggest proximity gain to date.<span class=\"pg\">p.204–205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Explicitly stakes a claim on his loyalty; wraps the old-test secret as mutual-trust bonding.<span class=\"pg\">p.216, 235<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p181-1\">← Before: Rooftop unmasking &amp; the sexual assault blackmail frame<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p236-1\">→ After: The podium &amp; &quot;I really hate you&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p236-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo the podium    i really hate you  takes the classroom podium the day before the exam to distribute the printed old test sheets   the role neither horikita nor ak could play  total class attention  even sudou stops   actually  these are the old test problems  i got them from a third year student last night   the cover story lands perfectly   yes  to tell you the truth  i heard that the midterm test from the year before last had almost exactly the same problems as this one  so  if we study what s on this test  it ll surely come in handy  downplays her own role when horikita praises her   i just did it for my friends  it was nothing special  cornered by horikita s direct  you hate me  don t you  drops the pretense entirely and admits it with her smile intact   ha ha  you got me     that s right  i really hate you   do you want me to tell you the reason   offering the reason unprompted   refused  public relations genius   weaponized honesty  delivers the class s salvation from the podium while openly confirming hatred to her partner in the same afternoon  the relationship s true baseline established  confessed mutual hatred under a functioning alliance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The podium &amp; &quot;I really hate you&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.236–238<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Actually, these are the old test problems. I got them from a third-year student last night.” (the cover story lands perfectly)<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yes. To tell you the truth, I heard that the midterm test from the year before last had almost exactly the same problems as this one. So, if we study what’s on this test, it’ll surely come in handy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I just did it for my friends. It was nothing special,”<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes the classroom podium the day before the exam to distribute the printed old-test sheets — the role neither Horikita nor AK could play; total class attention (even Sudou stops).<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Downplays her own role when Horikita praises her.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Cornered by Horikita&#x27;s direct &quot;You hate me, don&#x27;t you?&quot;, drops the pretense entirely and admits it with her smile intact.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ha ha, you got me.” … “That’s right. I really hate you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you want me to tell you the reason?” (offering the reason unprompted — refused)<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Public-relations genius + weaponized honesty: delivers the class&#x27;s salvation from the podium while openly confirming hatred to her partner in the same afternoon.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The relationship&#x27;s true baseline established: confessed mutual hatred under a functioning alliance.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p204-1\">← Before: Class A partnership, the ally test &amp; the secret bond<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p246-1\">→ After: Relief at the results<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p246-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo relief at the results shares a glance and sighs of relief with ayanokoji at the posted results   until the red line appears","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Relief at the results<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.246<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Shares a glance and sighs of relief with Ayanokōji at the posted results — until the red line appears.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p236-1\">← Before: The podium &amp; &quot;I really hate you&quot;<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p256-1\">→ After: The Class A recruitment pitch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p256-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo the class a recruitment pitch praises ayanokoji s plain dorm room on request  it s simple  but it feels nice and clean   everything was thanks to horikita san s efforts  she tutored ike  yamauchi  and sudou   deflects credit onto horikita in front of the trio  escalates the gathering  reveals the class a project to ike  yamauchi  and sudou and formally recruits them as helpers   we re all friends here  after all  horikita san  ayanokouji kun  and i are all working together to get into class a  if you re okay with it  i want you three to help us   yes  i absolutely am  increasing our points is an inevitable part of getting to the top as well  proverb war   a single arrow is easily broken  but not ten in a bundle    then  after horikita knocks the trio down   w well how about this  three heads are better than one  or something like that   if we keep going back and forth like this  though  we won t get anywhere  it s definitely better for us to get along   forces the truce that lands the recruits  morale engine  every time horikita demoralizes the trio  kushida rebuilds them   the recruitment pairing that makes the group functional","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p256-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The Class A recruitment pitch<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.256–261<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Everything was thanks to Horikita-san’s efforts. She tutored Ike, Yamauchi, and Sudou.” (deflects credit onto Horikita in front of the trio)<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“We’re all friends here, after all. Horikita-san, Ayanokouji-kun, and I are all working together to get into Class A. If you’re okay with it, I want you three to help us,”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yes. I absolutely am. Increasing our points is an inevitable part of getting to the top as well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Praises Ayanokōji&#x27;s plain dorm room on request (&quot;It’s simple, but it feels nice and clean.&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Escalates the gathering: reveals the Class A project to Ike, Yamauchi, and Sudou and formally recruits them as helpers.<span class=\"pg\">p.258–259<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Proverb war: “A single arrow is easily broken, but not ten in a bundle,” — then, after Horikita knocks the trio down: “W-well how about this? Three heads are better than one! Or something like that,”<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we keep going back and forth like this, though, we won’t get anywhere. It’s definitely better for us to get along.” (forces the truce that lands the recruits)<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Morale engine: every time Horikita demoralizes the trio, Kushida rebuilds them — the recruitment pairing that makes the group functional.<span class=\"pg\">p.256–261<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v1-p246-1\">← Before: Relief at the results<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p19-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 2  2 2  the social ceiling  narrated ak s snapshot of her position   she s extremely popular and has many friends  both girls and boys  she gets in person invitations  along with constant invites over the phone and through email  when she eats with friends she appears to have a real life","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.2: the social ceiling, narrated<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.19<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> AK&#x27;s snapshot of her position: &quot;She’s extremely popular and has many friends, both girls and boys. She gets in-person invitations, along with constant invites over the phone and through email... when she eats with friends she appears to have a real life.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p24-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: group-chat wistfulness<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p24-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 2  2 3  group chat wistfulness kushida was the one who doubted horikita would ever join the class group chat after the midterm invite  kushida had doubted whether horikita would actually participate  since she hated talking with others","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.3: group-chat wistfulness<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.24<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida was the one who doubted Horikita would ever join the class group chat after the midterm invite (&quot;Kushida had doubted whether Horikita would actually participate, since she hated talking with others.&quot;).<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p19-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the social ceiling, narrated<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p27-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: Sudou&#x27;s crisis conference — angel mode with an icy seam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p27-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 2  2 4  sudou s crisis conference   angel mode with an icy seam knocks during ak s kettle moment   kushida  the madonna of class d  poked her head through the entrance  she looked as cute as ever   oh  sudou kun s already here   yeah  i do  that s so we can meet up here  wait  did you not know about that  ayanokouji kun   she also holds a duplicate key to his room   assumed he d consented   umm  well should i return it to you   apologetically offers the key back   s suspended   oh  i got it  ayanokouji kun  he viciously beat chabashira sensei and then he spit on her   ha ha  i m only joking  sudou kun wouldn t go that far   the joke lands wrong   sudou s shock proves the secret is real   just wait a minute  sudou kun  can you please start over  and go a bit more slowly   a regular player  that s amazing  sudou kun  congratulations   still  that s amazing  we ve only just started school   so then they painted you as the bad guy  sudou kun   if class c started this  then sudou kun isn t at fault   we should tell chabashira sensei tomorrow  we should tell her it wasn t sudou kun s fault   sudou kun  you didn t lie to the teacher  did you  i mean  it seems strange  they didn t believe you even though you said you didn t do anything wrong  right   i guess that their plan is to severely punish sudou for punching them  huh   let s just come out and ask those three class c students to be honest  if they feel like what they did was wrong  then surely they d feel guilty about it  right   there are two ways we can prove your innocence  sudou kun  the first way is to simply get those boys in class c to admit that they lied  since you weren t at fault  it s probably best to get them to acknowledge that   the other idea is to find the eyewitness you talked about  sudou kun  if someone happened to see the fight  then we should be able to get to the heart of the matter   asking people one by one  or we could simply address each class as a whole   h huh  you don t want us to tell anyone   but won t the students in class c talk about how sudou kun was violent  i mean  that would work in their favor  i d think   sudou kun  i think it would be better if you kept your distance   sudou must stay away while accused   i don t think it s being dumped on us  we want you to rely on us  sudou kun  i don t know how much we can do  but we ll try our best  okay   i have a few things i wanted to talk to you about  ayanokouji kun  you didn t seem very enthusiastic about helping sudou kun   maybe  but sudou kun came to you  ayanokouji kun  he came to you before horikita san  hirata kun  or even ike kun  the mask slips mid conversation   for an instant  kushida s glare turned icy  which perplexed me    then she recomposes into advice   i think it might be better if you made more effort to blend in  ayanokouji kun   of course  we re friends  so what will you do  ayanokouji kun   do you think horikita san will help us   i know that you re trying to dodge the question  but you ll help  too  won t you  ayanokouji kun   you won t be useless  i m sure you ll be useful  somehow   so what should we do  sudou kun said that it wouldn t help  but i think it d be good to talk with the three students he fought  to tell you the truth  i m friends with komiya kun and the others  therefore  it might be possible to persuade them  hmm  it may be dangerous  though   well then  i guess looking for the eyewitness is our best bet  structured empathy  jokes to defuse  then imposes an agenda  two proof routes  volunteers her cross class network  komiya et al  in c  as a tool  and pins ak to a commitment he keeps dodging  her pressure only works socially   ak admits  like right now  i didn t have the guts to promise that i d help  her icy glare is the only lever that lands  officially takes his side  secures his cooperation with warmth  keeps the secrecy bargain  escalates one on one after sudou leaves  demands he publicly invest in the case  he internally recalls her  i hate you  warning while complying outwardly","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.4: Sudou&#x27;s crisis conference — angel mode with an icy seam<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.27–38<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Knocks during AK&#x27;s kettle moment; &quot;Kushida, the Madonna of Class D, poked her head through the entrance. She looked as cute as ever.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Oh, Sudou-kun’s already here,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yeah, I do. That’s so we can meet up here… Wait, did you not know about that, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot; (she also holds a duplicate key to his room — assumed he&#x27;d consented)<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Umm, well…should I return it to you?&quot; (apologetically offers the key back)<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>33 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;S-suspended?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, I got it, Ayanokouji-kun. He viciously beat Chabashira-sensei and then he spit on her!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ha ha, I’m only joking! Sudou-kun wouldn’t go that far.&quot; (the joke lands wrong — Sudou&#x27;s shock proves the secret is real)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Just wait a minute, Sudou-kun. Can you please start over, and go a bit more slowly?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;A regular player? That’s amazing, Sudou-kun! Congratulations!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Still, that’s amazing. We’ve only just started school.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So then they painted you as the bad guy, Sudou-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If Class C started this, then Sudou-kun isn’t at fault.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We should tell Chabashira-sensei tomorrow. We should tell her it wasn’t Sudou-kun’s fault,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sudou-kun, you didn’t lie to the teacher, did you? I mean, it seems strange. They didn’t believe you even though you said you didn’t do anything wrong. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I guess that their plan is to severely punish Sudou for punching them, huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Let’s just come out and ask those three Class C students to be honest. If they feel like what they did was wrong, then surely they’d feel guilty about it. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There are two ways we can prove your innocence, Sudou-kun. The first way is to simply get those boys in Class C to admit that they lied. Since you weren’t at fault, it’s probably best to get them to acknowledge that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The other idea is to find the eyewitness you talked about, Sudou-kun. If someone happened to see the fight, then we should be able to get to the heart of the matter.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Asking people one by one? Or we could simply address each class as a whole,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;H-huh? You don’t want us to tell anyone?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But won’t the students in Class C talk about how Sudou-kun was violent? I mean, that would work in their favor, I’d think.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sudou-kun, I think it would be better if you kept your distance,&quot; (Sudou must stay away while accused)<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t think it’s being dumped on us. We want you to rely on us, Sudou-kun. I don’t know how much we can do, but we’ll try our best. Okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have a few things I wanted to talk to you about, Ayanokouji-kun. You didn’t seem very enthusiastic about helping Sudou-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Maybe, but Sudou-kun came to you, Ayanokouji-kun. He came to you before Horikita-san, Hirata-kun, or even Ike-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The mask slips mid-conversation: &quot;For an instant, Kushida’s glare turned icy, which perplexed me.&quot; — then she recomposes into advice.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I think it might be better if you made more effort to blend in, Ayanokouji-kun,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Of course. We’re friends. So what will you do, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you think Horikita-san will help us?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I know that you’re trying to dodge the question, but you’ll help, too. Won’t you, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You won’t be useless. I’m sure you’ll be useful, somehow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So what should we do? Sudou-kun said that it wouldn’t help, but I think it’d be good to talk with the three students he fought. To tell you the truth, I’m friends with Komiya-kun and the others. Therefore, it might be possible to persuade them. Hmm, it may be dangerous, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well then, I guess looking for the eyewitness is our best bet.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Structured empathy: jokes to defuse, then imposes an agenda (two proof routes), volunteers her cross-class network (Komiya et al. in C) as a tool, and pins AK to a commitment he keeps dodging.<span class=\"pg\">p.29–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Her pressure only works socially — AK admits &quot;Like right now, I didn’t have the guts to promise that I’d help.&quot;; her icy glare is the only lever that lands.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Officially takes his side, secures his cooperation with warmth, keeps the secrecy bargain.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Escalates one-on-one after Sudou leaves; demands he publicly invest in the case; he internally recalls her &quot;I hate you&quot; warning while complying outwardly.<span class=\"pg\">p.36–38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p24-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: group-chat wistfulness<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p41-1\">→ After: Ch.3 open: she takes the class&#x27;s anger apart in front of everyone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p41-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 3 open  she takes the class s anger apart in front of everyone with the uproar starting to get out of hand  ak s note on her motive   naturally  kushida didn t want this to happen    she is defending the class s cohesion  not sudou   everyone  can you please listen to what i have to say   what our teacher said seems to be true  sudou kun may have been in a fight  however  sudou kun was dragged into it  she tells the room sudou s whole account   the regular player nomination  the envious clubmates  the threat  the self defence   kushida conveyed yesterday s story to the whole class   i d like to ask you all again  if anyone knows someone who saw what happened  whether it s someone in class  a friend  or an upperclassman  please tell me  you can contact me at any time  i would sincerely appreciate it  ak measures the difference between her and the teacher saying the same thing   even though she d basically said the same thing as chabashira sensei  the class had a very different response  she had an innate ability to connect with people  her presence glowed so bright that i could almost feel it  charisma alone does not carry it  after yamauchi s accusation   kushida s appeal for sudou s innocence didn t seem to have reached anyone  it takes hirata standing up   and then karuizawa   to turn the room  he backs her appeal publicly  ak credits the pair of them plus karuizawa with converting the class  which is the closest the volume comes to the two leaders acting together  ak s paired mechanism  stated in the same breath   if kushida lived by the softness of her heart  then karuizawa lived by the strength of her will","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p41-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 open: she takes the class&#x27;s anger apart in front of everyone<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.41–43<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">With the uproar starting to get out of hand, AK&#x27;s note on her motive: &quot;Naturally, Kushida didn’t want this to happen.&quot; — she is defending the class&#x27;s cohesion, not Sudou. She tells the room Sudou&#x27;s whole account — the regular-player nomination, the envious clubmates, the threat, the self-defence: &quot;Kushida conveyed yesterday’s story to the whole class.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Everyone, can you please listen to what I have to say?”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What our teacher said seems to be true. Sudou-kun may have been in a fight. However, Sudou-kun was dragged into it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’d like to ask you all again. If anyone knows someone who saw what happened, whether it’s someone in class, a friend, or an upperclassman, please tell me. You can contact me at any time. I would sincerely appreciate it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> AK measures the difference between her and the teacher saying the same thing: &quot;Even though she’d basically said the same thing as Chabashira-sensei, the class had a very different response. She had an innate ability to connect with people. Her presence glowed so bright that I could almost feel it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Charisma alone does not carry it: after Yamauchi&#x27;s accusation, &quot;Kushida’s appeal for Sudou’s innocence didn’t seem to have reached anyone.&quot; It takes Hirata standing up — and then Karuizawa — to turn the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> He backs her appeal publicly; AK credits the pair of them plus Karuizawa with converting the class, which is the closest the volume comes to the two leaders acting together.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> AK&#x27;s paired mechanism, stated in the same breath: &quot;If Kushida lived by the softness of her heart, then Karuizawa lived by the strength of her will.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p27-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: Sudou&#x27;s crisis conference — angel mode with an icy seam<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p44-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: keeping Ayanokōji inside the group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p44-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 3  3 1  keeping ayanokoji inside the group she assembles the lunch table   ak  horikita  ike  yamauchi  sudou   by asking him directly   when lunchtime came  kushida had invited me with a smile  she d said   want to get lunch  i d said okay  of course  i mean  i didn t have any choice in the matter  she leaves the table early to work her own network   ah  sorry  i have to go for a bit  i m going to try asking my upperclassmen friends if they saw anything","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p44-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.1: keeping Ayanokōji inside the group<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.44, p.47<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She assembles the lunch table — AK, Horikita, Ike, Yamauchi, Sudou — by asking him directly: &quot;When lunchtime came, Kushida had invited me with a smile. She’d said, &#x27;Want to get lunch?&#x27; I’d said okay, of course. I mean, I didn’t have any choice in the matter.&quot; She leaves the table early to work her own network: “Ah, sorry. I have to go for a bit. I’m going to try asking my upperclassmen friends if they saw anything.”<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p41-1\">← Before: Ch.3 open: she takes the class&#x27;s anger apart in front of everyone<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2–3.3: Horikita, the lesson, and Class B<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p54-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 3  3 2 3 3  horikita  the lesson  and class b  are you really heading back  horikita san   you will help us out  won t you   stopping ak from slipping out  ak   i couldn t refuse  slightly upturned eyes   pleading   lethal   i want to get horikita san to help us out this time  can you try asking her again   yeah  i want to chase after her  if horikita san helps  i think she ll make a big difference  she takes ak s arm in front of ike and yamauchi and walks him out with her  ike and yamauchi are left behind because  as ak notes   you certainly couldn t claim those two were friendly with horikita   i really want you to help us with sudou s case  is that possible   i know you did  but but  i think this is necessary to reach class a   w wait  what do you mean  wasn t sudou kun dragged into the fight   sudou kun is a perpetrator  is that true   i don t agree with abandoning sudou kun just to punish him  if she s dissatisfied with him  i think she should at least talk to him directly  that s what friends would do   okay  i understand  i ll follow your advice  ayanokouji kun  ak s definition of her  offered as a limit on himself   she would extend her hand to a friend in need as many times as it took  it sounds simple  but it was actually difficult  only someone like kushida could do such a thing  she is moved mid conversation and lets it show   kushida arched her back and stretched  i d changed her thinking    then converts the new position into action  okay  let s go hunt for the witness   no  i m sorry  i failed   well then  let s go to class b right away   i also think you re being too negative  i do think it s a good idea to ask class b  but i also think we should ask several people at once  if not  we may not find the witness in time   i m sorry  ayanokouji kun   overruling his one at a time plan with ike and yamauchi behind her  and apologising for it  ak withdraws   kushida s plan had convinced me  so i withdrew my own  in the class b room she is the only one of the four who moves   kushida was the only one who remained unfazed  in fact  she found her class b friends and  with a smile on her face  waved to them and headed over  ak s note on the transferability of her manner   she chatted with people regardless of gender  exactly how she acted in class d  no one was more jealous of this than ike and yamauchi  she pitches sudou s case to the roughly ten class b students still in the room   the first cross class advocacy of the volume  her network has a ceiling she cannot see  ak s whole plan for class b rests on the class s self interest  and she is running on friendship  which is why the report she brings back surprises him   what the report is  the text withholds until the next chapter","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.2–3.3: Horikita, the lesson, and Class B<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.54–63<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She takes AK&#x27;s arm in front of Ike and Yamauchi and walks him out with her; Ike and Yamauchi are left behind because, as AK notes, &quot;You certainly couldn’t claim those two were friendly with Horikita.&quot; In the Class B room she is the only one of the four who moves: &quot;Kushida was the only one who remained unfazed. In fact, she found her Class B friends and, with a smile on her face, waved to them and headed over.&quot; She pitches Sudou&#x27;s case to the roughly ten Class B students still in the room — the first cross-class advocacy of the volume.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Are you really heading back? Horikita-san?”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You will…help us out, won’t you?” (stopping AK from slipping out; AK: &quot;I couldn’t refuse. Slightly upturned eyes + pleading = lethal.&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I want to get Horikita-san to help us out this time. Can you try asking her again?”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. I want to chase after her. If Horikita-san helps, I think she’ll make a big difference.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I really want you to help us with Sudou’s case. Is that possible?”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know you did, but…but, I think this is necessary to reach Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “W-wait. What do you mean? Wasn’t Sudou-kun dragged into the fight?”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sudou-kun is a perpetrator? Is that…true?”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t agree with abandoning Sudou-kun just to punish him. If she’s dissatisfied with him, I think she should at least talk to him directly. That’s what friends would do.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. I understand. I’ll follow your advice, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s definition of her, offered as a limit on himself: &quot;She would extend her hand to a friend in need as many times as it took. It sounds simple, but it was actually difficult. Only someone like Kushida could do such a thing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She is moved mid-conversation and lets it show: &quot;Kushida arched her back and stretched; I’d changed her thinking.&quot; — then converts the new position into action (&quot;Okay, let’s go hunt for the witness.&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I’m sorry. I failed,”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then, let’s go to Class B right away!”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I also think you’re being too negative. I do think it’s a good idea to ask Class B, but I also think we should ask several people at once. If not, we may not find the witness in time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, Ayanokouji-kun.” (overruling his one-at-a-time plan with Ike and Yamauchi behind her, and apologising for it; AK withdraws: &quot;Kushida’s plan had convinced me, so I withdrew my own.&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> AK&#x27;s note on the transferability of her manner: &quot;She chatted with people regardless of gender, exactly how she acted in Class D. No one was more jealous of this than Ike and Yamauchi.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Her network has a ceiling she cannot see: AK&#x27;s whole plan for Class B rests on the class&#x27;s self-interest, and she is running on friendship, which is why the report she brings back surprises him. (What the report is, the text withholds until the next chapter.)<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p44-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: keeping Ayanokōji inside the group<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p66-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: she runs the search, and is the only one who can name Sakura&#x27;s seat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p66-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 4  4 0 4 1  she runs the search  and is the only one who can name sakura s seat  as long as we can find a witness  it s not impossible  let s keep trying our best  ike kun    the pep line she gives the boy who has just declared the case hopeless  her method of remembering is exact   it s certainly true that sudou kun didn t say he saw anyone  he said that he had a feeling that someone was there    she corrects the class s summary of a claim three days old  she re engineers the search from the witness to the witness s surroundings   we might want to change our methods a little  for example  let s look for someone who might have found a witness    ak s judgement   that wasn t a bad idea  horikita arrives at the room and kushida is the reason she stays   kushida peered over at the entrance  probably concerned that horikita wouldn t return   ah  horikita san  kushida said  kushida smiled and waved to horikita   if you didn t come here to help  then why did you come    and then  instead of pressing   well  i m happy if you just want to listen to us talk  i hoped you could give some advice  she is the class s map of itself   no  you re both wrong  she sits diagonally ahead of sudou kun to the right    ak   kushida corrected them  a slightly pouty look on her face  she defends a classmate she has never spoken to  in public  against ike   it s not good to remember people based on something like that  ikekun  that s pathetic  the phone attempt fails and she names why it is a delicate thing   no luck  the call didn t go through  i can try again later  but this may be a delicate matter  and  she gave me her contact information  but she doesn t know me very well  she might be confused if i tried to call her  she reads the room s failure before it happens and shrinks the plan to one person   well  i ll try to talk to her myself tomorrow  i think she might be on her guard if a lot of people approach her  she holds sakura s number and sakura s seating position and none of sakura s trust  and is the one student whose name she will not let ike reduce to a body","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: she runs the search, and is the only one who can name Sakura&#x27;s seat<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.66–82<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita arrives at the room and Kushida is the reason she stays: &quot;Kushida peered over at the entrance, probably concerned that Horikita wouldn’t return. &#x27;Ah, Horikita-san!&#x27; Kushida said. Kushida smiled and waved to Horikita.&quot; She is the class&#x27;s map of itself: &quot;No, you’re both wrong. She sits diagonally ahead of Sudou-kun to the right.&quot; — AK: &quot;Kushida corrected them, a slightly pouty look on her face.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;As long as we can find a witness, it’s not impossible. Let’s keep trying our best, Ike-kun.&quot; — the pep line she gives the boy who has just declared the case hopeless.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">She re-engineers the search from the witness to the witness&#x27;s surroundings: &quot;We might want to change our methods a little. For example, let’s look for someone who might have found a witness.&quot; — AK&#x27;s judgement: &quot;That wasn’t a bad…<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you didn’t come here to help, then why did you come?&quot; — and then, instead of pressing: &quot;Well, I’m happy if you just want to listen to us talk. I hoped you could give some advice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Her method of remembering is exact: &quot;It’s certainly true that Sudou-kun didn’t say he saw anyone. He said that he had a feeling that someone was there.&quot; — she corrects the class&#x27;s summary of a claim three days old.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She re-engineers the search from the witness to the witness&#x27;s surroundings: &quot;We might want to change our methods a little. For example, let’s look for someone who might have found a witness.&quot; — AK&#x27;s judgement: &quot;That wasn’t a bad idea.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She defends a classmate she has never spoken to, in public, against Ike: &quot;It’s not good to remember people based on something like that, Ikekun! That’s pathetic.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The phone attempt fails and she names why it is a delicate thing: &quot;No luck. The call didn’t go through. I can try again later, but this may be a delicate matter.&quot; and &quot;She gave me her contact information, but she doesn’t know me very well. She might be confused if I tried to call her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She reads the room&#x27;s failure before it happens and shrinks the plan to one person: &quot;Well, I’ll try to talk to her myself tomorrow. I think she might be on her guard if a lot of people approach her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> She holds Sakura&#x27;s number and Sakura&#x27;s seating position and none of Sakura&#x27;s trust, and is the one student whose name she will not let Ike reduce to a body.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2–3.3: Horikita, the lesson, and Class B<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p86-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: the approach fails in front of the whole class<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p86-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 4  4 2 4 3  the approach fails in front of the whole class  class was over  kushida stood up right as homeroom ended and walked over towards sakura  who was quietly preparing to leave  kushida seemed oddly nervous   sakura san  then  i wanted to ask you something  sakura san  do you have a moment  it s about sudou s case   can you please make some time  this is important  so i d like to talk to you  when sudou kun was involved in the incident  were you perhaps somewhere nearby   can t you please spare just a few minutes now    the third ask  the one that turns the conversation into a scene the room is watching  ak s post mortem of her judgement  in her own terms   kushida probably had expected this conversation to go more smoothly  and had gone into this situation thinking she wasn t going to be rejected  that explained why this was currently falling apart  she takes the blame for a broken camera that was not hers   i i m sorry  it s because i came up and talked to you so suddenly  that    and is answered flatly   no  that s not it  i was just careless  that s all  anyway  goodbye  even after failing she keeps the case alive by asking the quietest boy in the room   ayanokouji kun  you re sudou kun s ally  aren t you     well  it s just that things seem to a bit tense  everyone s desire to save sudou is fading  she uses his proximity as a resource twice in one day  the ally question  and the earlier instruction that he keep horikita reachable  hirata briefs ak about her because  she doesn t talk to anyone except for you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p86-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: the approach fails in front of the whole class<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.86–93<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">&quot;Class was over. Kushida stood up right as homeroom ended and walked over towards Sakura, who was quietly preparing to leave. Kushida seemed oddly nervous.&quot; She takes the blame for a broken camera that was not hers: &quot;I-I’m sorry. It’s because I came up and talked to you so suddenly, that…&quot; — and is answered flatly: &quot;No, that’s not it. I was just careless, that’s all… Anyway, goodbye.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sakura-san?&quot; then &quot;I wanted to ask you something, Sakura-san. Do you have a moment? It’s about Sudou’s case.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Can you please make some time? This is important, so I’d like to talk to you. When Sudou-kun was involved in the incident, were you perhaps somewhere nearby?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Can’t you please spare just a few minutes now?&quot; — the third ask, the one that turns the conversation into a scene the room is watching.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> AK&#x27;s post-mortem of her judgement, in her own terms: &quot;Kushida probably had expected this conversation to go more smoothly, and had gone into this situation thinking she wasn’t going to be rejected. That explained why this was currently falling apart.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Even after failing she keeps the case alive by asking the quietest boy in the room: &quot;Ayanokouji-kun, you’re Sudou-kun’s ally, aren’t you?&quot; — &quot;Well, it’s just that things seem to a bit tense. Everyone’s desire to save Sudou is fading.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She uses his proximity as a resource twice in one day: the ally question, and the earlier instruction that he keep Horikita reachable (Hirata briefs AK about her because &quot;she doesn’t talk to anyone except for you&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p66-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0–4.1: she runs the search, and is the only one who can name Sakura&#x27;s seat<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p128-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.8: she phones him at night, and cannot finish what she starts<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p128-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 4  4 8  she phones him at night  and cannot finish what she starts the first time she reaches him unbidden  after ten   i m sorry for calling you so late  you re still up  she asked   sakura san s digital camera was broken  right  i feel like i m partially to blame since i made her so flustered  so i wanted to take responsibility for that   yeah  she seemed hesitant at first  but then said that she d be fine with the day after tomorrow  i think that sakura s digital camera is probably really important to her   if we were just going to get it repaired  i suppose  but  there s another thing  i d like your help with it  ayanokouji kun  what horikita has concluded  carried by the one person horikita will not speak to   horikita san seems convinced that sakura saw everything  after getting a bit closer to sakura san  i also think she knows something  but there has to be some reason why she s keeping quiet  since she keeps denying that she witnessed it   that reminds me  it was really scary when kouenji kun and sudoukun looked like they were about to start fighting    printed as one word  kept as the translation has it   i couldn t even move  hirata kun was so amazing  though   class d was able to come together  thanks to you and hirata  the fact that the boys and girls are separated plays a big part  too   speaking of special  don t you think that horikita san is way more special than someone like me  she s great at studying and excels at sports  it makes me wonder why she s in class d   but doesn t she behave normally with you  ayanokouji kun   huh  ah  yeah  it is  why  what about it    he has asked whether her room is on the ninth floor  her gift with the class s outliers  described from the outside   kushida had done a wonderful job taking the proper first steps to earn sakura s trust  the only silence the volume records her in   suddenly  kushida fell silent  it was unexpected silence  without warning  our conversation  which had been smooth up until now  came to a screeching halt  she starts a confession three times and stops   hey  then  i if  well  i  i  then  no  it s nothing    and the recorder s verdict   that sure didn t seem like nothing   well  i ll see you the day after tomorrow  ayanokouji kun    the call s last line  with the unfinished one still in the air  she is the only classmate who tests his account of horikita instead of accepting it   and his reaction to being read is discomfort rather than deflection   i didn t like being misunderstood by kushida  she hesitates immediately after being asked for her floor number  and the volume never says whether the two are connected  what is recorded is only the sequence  the question  the halt  the swallowed sentence  the goodbye","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p128-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.8: she phones him at night, and cannot finish what she starts<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.128–131<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The first time she reaches him unbidden, after ten: &quot;I’m sorry for calling you so late. You’re still up?&quot; she asked.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sakura-san’s digital camera was broken, right? I feel like I’m partially to blame since I made her so flustered. So I wanted to take responsibility for that…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yeah. She seemed hesitant at first, but then said that she’d be fine with the day after tomorrow. I think that Sakura’s digital camera is probably really important to her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If we were just going to get it repaired, I suppose. But, there’s another thing. I’d like your help with it, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> What Horikita has concluded, carried by the one person Horikita will not speak to: &quot;Horikita-san seems convinced that Sakura saw everything. After getting a bit closer to Sakura-san, I also think she knows something. But there has to be some reason why she’s keeping quiet, since she keeps denying that she witnessed it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That reminds me. It was really scary when Kouenji-kun and Sudoukun looked like they were about to start fighting.&quot; — printed as one word; kept as the translation has it.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I couldn’t even move. Hirata-kun was so amazing, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Class D was able to come together, thanks to you and Hirata. The fact that the boys and girls are separated plays a big part, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Speaking of special, don’t you think that Horikita-san is way more special than someone like me? She’s great at studying and excels at sports. It makes me wonder why she’s in Class D.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But doesn’t she behave normally with you, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Huh? Ah, yeah, it is. Why? What about it?&quot; — he has asked whether her room is on the ninth floor.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Her gift with the class&#x27;s outliers, described from the outside: &quot;Kushida had done a wonderful job taking the proper first steps to earn Sakura’s trust.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The only silence the volume records her in: &quot;Suddenly, Kushida fell silent. It was unexpected silence, without warning. Our conversation, which had been smooth up until now, came to a screeching halt.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> She starts a confession three times and stops: &quot;Hey—&quot; then &quot;I-If… Well… I… I—&quot; then &quot;No, it’s nothing.&quot; — and the recorder&#x27;s verdict: &quot;That sure didn’t seem like nothing…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, I’ll see you the day after tomorrow, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; — the call&#x27;s last line, with the unfinished one still in the air.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She is the only classmate who tests his account of Horikita instead of accepting it — and his reaction to being read is discomfort rather than deflection: &quot;I didn’t like being misunderstood by Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130–131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She hesitates immediately after being asked for her floor number, and the volume never says whether the two are connected. What is recorded is only the sequence: the question, the halt, the swallowed sentence, the goodbye.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p86-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: the approach fails in front of the whole class<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p132-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.9–4.10: how she works on someone who cannot be worked on<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p132-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 4  4 9 4 10  how she works on someone who cannot be worked on  good morning  and  sorry  were you waiting long   this is the first time we ve met up on a day off  it s refreshing  the opening test of whether he has been excluded from his own class   weren t you really busy during your downtime last week  i m glad that you came despite that  ayanokouji kun    then  precisely   i m talking about ike kun and the others going to that cafe  of course   by any chance   i didn t mean anything  i m sorry  i guess i said something wrong    and when he says he does not care   you do seem to care   no  no  that s not true at all  i think we re great together    to his  i think i might look a little out of place next to you   you re that surprisingly delicate  ayanokouji kun  i don t really care what others say  i don t think it s an insult at all  i really think we suit each other   she asked me to invite you  ayanokouji kun  didn t sakura san contact you    sakura s invitation came through kushida  and kushida did not know he had not been contacted directly   right now  how about we sit and wait   let s see  i m sure they have a repair counter somewhere  let s check it out   there it is  the repairs counter   what s the matter  sakura san    she is the only one of the three who asks about sakura s fear out loud  the transaction as an act of translation   kushida s worldly wisdom was certainly impressive  even though it was her first time meeting the store clerk  she was soon talking to him as if they were longtime friends  she reads the clerk s interest and manages it without refusing him   in order to conclude their business  she urged sakura to hand over the camera   that clerk sure was something else  he talked with such incredible passion  i was just so shocked   n no  i wasn t disgusted by him  do you know something  about that clerk    the question that lets sakura say she was afraid   did you know about this  ayanokouji kun     kushida seemed to have an epiphany  she turned to me with wide eyes   you really looked out for sakura san   oh  no need to thank me  and then  sakura san  you really like your camera  don t you   i think being knowledgeable and liking things are separate matters  it s wonderful to be so passionate about something   sakura san  have we met somewhere before     kushida murmured  the ask that sakura refuses   sorry  it s just that when i look at you  i get this feeling that we ve met before  sakura san  hey  weird question  but could you try removing your glasses   we should hang out together again  sakura san  not just with me  but with my other friends  too  her offer of a normal relationship  phrased as a complaint about speech   you can talk to us normally  you know  if it s okay with you  we re in the same grade  it sounds a little weird when you speak so formally to us   it s not really a bad thing  i mean  i d be happy if you didn t speak so formally to me  though   it s okay  though  you don t need to force yourself  the ask that finally gets the witness   so  does that mean that you saw sudou kun fight with those other students  and then  no  we do  why did you decide to tell us now  though  i mean  i m happy you did  but i don t want you to force yourself  you don t have to do this just because you re grateful  you know   is that really true  you re not forcing yourself  kushida asked    the same question twice in one minute  because the first answer was a shake of the head   thank you  sakura san  i m sure sudou kun will be really happy     kushida took sakura s hand  the case the whole class failed to move in three weeks is closed by a hand hold and two refusals to press   i wondered if a new friendship had been born right here  right now  at any rate  we had sudou s witness  she is the only person in class d who gets things done by being with people rather than by being right about them  the volume records her succeeding at exactly the task horikita wrote off as worthless  from a camera knocked over in a classroom  p 90  to a promise to testify in a shopping mall  the whole distance is crossed by kushida refusing to make anything harder than it already is  she recruits him by asking  tests whether he has been left out of his own friend group  and lets him fill in a form  he is her one witness that she is capable of a plain conversation  her instinct to close on sakura stops short of the truth  she asks about the glasses  gets refused  and  kushida seemed to feel that it would make trouble if she pressed the issue  so she kept quiet  or rather  she didn t ask anything else","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p132-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.9–4.10: how she works on someone who cannot be worked on<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.132–145<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Good morning!&quot; and &quot;Sorry. Were you waiting long?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;This is the first time we’ve met up on a day off. It’s refreshing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">The opening test of whether he has been excluded from his own class: &quot;Weren’t you really busy during your downtime last week? I’m glad that you came despite that, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; — then, precisely: &quot;I’m talking about Ike-kun and…<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>32 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The opening test of whether he has been excluded from his own class: &quot;Weren’t you really busy during your downtime last week? I’m glad that you came despite that, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; — then, precisely: &quot;I’m talking about Ike-kun and the others going to that café, of course.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;By any chance…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I didn’t mean anything… I’m sorry, I guess I said something wrong…&quot; — and when he says he does not care: &quot;You do seem to care…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, no, that’s not true at all. I think we’re great together,&quot; — to his &quot;I think I might look a little out of place next to you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re that surprisingly delicate, Ayanokouji-kun? I don’t really care what others say. I don’t think it’s an insult at all. I really think we suit each other.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;She asked me to invite you, Ayanokouji-kun. Didn’t Sakura-san contact you?&quot; — Sakura&#x27;s invitation came through Kushida, and Kushida did not know he had not been contacted directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Right now, how about we sit and wait?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Let’s see, I’m sure they have a repair counter somewhere. Let’s check it out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There it is! The repairs counter.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What’s the matter, Sakura-san?&quot; — she is the only one of the three who asks about Sakura&#x27;s fear out loud.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The transaction as an act of translation: &quot;Kushida’s worldly wisdom was certainly impressive. Even though it was her first time meeting the store clerk, she was soon talking to him as if they were longtime friends.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She reads the clerk&#x27;s interest and manages it without refusing him: &quot;In order to conclude their business, she urged Sakura to hand over the camera.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That clerk sure was something else. He talked with such incredible passion, I was just so shocked,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;N-no, I wasn’t disgusted by him. Do you know something? About that clerk?&quot; — the question that lets Sakura say she was afraid.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Did you know about this, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot; — &quot;Kushida seemed to have an epiphany. She turned to me with wide eyes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You really looked out for Sakura-san,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, no need to thank me.&quot; and then &quot;Sakura-san, you really like your camera. Don’t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I think being knowledgeable and liking things are separate matters. It’s wonderful to be so passionate about something.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sakura-san, have we met somewhere before?&quot; — &quot;Kushida murmured.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The ask that Sakura refuses: &quot;Sorry. It’s just that when I look at you, I get this feeling that we’ve met before, Sakura-san. Hey, weird question, but could you try removing your glasses?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We should hang out together again, Sakura-san. Not just with me, but with my other friends, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her offer of a normal relationship, phrased as a complaint about speech: &quot;you can talk to us normally, you know? If it’s okay with you. We’re in the same grade. It sounds a little weird when you speak so formally to us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s not really a bad thing! I mean, I’d be happy if you didn’t speak so formally to me, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s okay, though. You don’t need to force yourself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The ask that finally gets the witness: &quot;So, does that mean that you saw Sudou-kun fight with those other students?&quot; and then &quot;No, we do. Why did you decide to tell us now, though? I mean, I’m happy you did, but I don’t want you to force yourself. You don’t have to do this just because you’re grateful, you know?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Is that really true? You’re not forcing yourself?&quot; Kushida asked. — the same question twice in one minute, because the first answer was a shake of the head.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Thank you, Sakura-san. I’m sure Sudou-kun will be really happy.&quot; — &quot;Kushida took Sakura’s hand.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The case the whole class failed to move in three weeks is closed by a hand-hold and two refusals to press: &quot;I wondered if a new friendship had been born right here, right now. At any rate, we had Sudou’s witness.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She is the only person in Class D who gets things done by being with people rather than by being right about them; the volume records her succeeding at exactly the task Horikita wrote off as worthless.<span class=\"pg\">p.132–146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> From a camera knocked over in a classroom (p.90) to a promise to testify in a shopping mall: the whole distance is crossed by Kushida refusing to make anything harder than it already is.<span class=\"pg\">p.138–146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She recruits him by asking, tests whether he has been left out of his own friend group, and lets him fill in a form; he is her one witness that she is capable of a plain conversation.<span class=\"pg\">p.128–145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Her instinct to close on Sakura stops short of the truth: she asks about the glasses, gets refused, and &quot;Kushida seemed to feel that it would make trouble if she pressed the issue, so she kept quiet. Or rather, she didn’t ask anything else.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p128-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.8: she phones him at night, and cannot finish what she starts<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p147-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.11: the same evening, on two calls<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p147-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 4  4 11  the same evening  on two calls  we got closer to sakura  but  is it really okay for me to say that    her voice on the phone that night  the translation leaves the reply s speaker untagged and it is not assigned  her reason for the glasses  which turns out not to be a reason   well  i mean  i thought saying so might be kind of cruel  but  i just feel like her glasses don t really suit her  for some reason  it s like she doesn t really need them  or something  i don t understand it myself  i also thought that we d met somewhere before  but that was probably just a misunderstanding   huh  sakura san wears fake glasses  but she said that her eyesight was really bad   appearing fashionable with glasses  hmm  that doesn t sound normal   there s that  wearing glasses does make you look smart   i knew it was right to bring you along  ayanokouji kun  i feel like you re very observant of people   oh  sure  sorry for talking so long    the line she says when he cuts her off to answer sakura   though there was a heavy regret in those parting words  she is asked whether sakura called her and did not receive the call   a few minutes later  kushida confirmed that she hadn t heard back from sakura  the volume leaves sakura s unfinished sentence on one side of the exchange and kushida s unfinished sentence on the other","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p147-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.11: the same evening, on two calls<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.147–150<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We got closer to Sakura, but… Is it really okay for me to say that?&quot; — her voice on the phone that night; the translation leaves the reply&#x27;s speaker untagged and it is not assigned.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Her reason for the glasses, which turns out not to be a reason: &quot;Well, I mean… I thought saying so might be kind of cruel, but… I just feel like her glasses don’t really suit her, for some reason. It’s like she doesn’t really…<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Huh? Sakura-san wears fake glasses? But she said that her eyesight was really bad…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her reason for the glasses, which turns out not to be a reason: &quot;Well, I mean… I thought saying so might be kind of cruel, but… I just feel like her glasses don’t really suit her, for some reason. It’s like she doesn’t really need them, or something. I don’t understand it myself. I also thought that we’d met somewhere before, but that was probably just a misunderstanding.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Appearing fashionable with glasses? Hmm, that doesn’t sound normal.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There’s that. Wearing glasses does make you look smart.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I knew it was right to bring you along, Ayanokouji-kun. I feel like you’re very observant of people.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, sure. Sorry for talking so long.&quot; — the line she says when he cuts her off to answer Sakura; &quot;Though there was a heavy regret in those parting words.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She is asked whether Sakura called her and did not receive the call: &quot;A few minutes later, Kushida confirmed that she hadn’t heard back from Sakura.&quot; The volume leaves Sakura&#x27;s unfinished sentence on one side of the exchange and Kushida&#x27;s unfinished sentence on the other.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p132-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.9–4.10: how she works on someone who cannot be worked on<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.1: she reads Horikita better than Horikita reads herself<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p159-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 5  5 1  she reads horikita better than horikita reads herself  good morning  ayanokouji kun   thanks for yesterday  you really saved me   let s hang out again sometime  okay  she does not come in  she  briefly peeked into the classroom  and calls him out to the hallway   i have a feeling i just saw something really incredible   that s not it  i think she feels alienated and lonely over not being invited   she probably doesn t know how she feels  i m sure she s probably noticed how much fun it is to spend time with friends and talk to them  though  that s a good thing  a good thing   perhaps you re realizing something fundamental  ayanokouji kun  horikita san is upset that you didn t invite her to come along  the reading is hers alone  the narrator calls it  a bizarre thought  and cannot accept it  she names horikita s feeling as loneliness while disliking her  and says it in the hallway where horikita cannot hear","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.1: she reads Horikita better than Horikita reads herself<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.159–162<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She does not come in; she &quot;briefly peeked into the classroom&quot; and calls him out to the hallway.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Good morning! Ayanokouji-kun!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Thanks for yesterday. You really saved me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Let’s hang out again sometime, okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have a feeling I just saw something really incredible!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That’s not it. I think she feels alienated and lonely over not being invited.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;She probably doesn’t know how she feels… I’m sure she’s probably noticed how much fun it is to spend time with friends and talk to them, though. That’s a good thing, a good thing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Perhaps you’re realizing something fundamental, Ayanokouji-kun. Horikita-san is upset that you didn’t invite her to come along.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The reading is hers alone; the narrator calls it &quot;a bizarre thought&quot; and cannot accept it.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She names Horikita&#x27;s feeling as loneliness while disliking her, and says it in the hallway where Horikita cannot hear.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p147-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.11: the same evening, on two calls<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p163-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: she brings the witness, then loses the seat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p163-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 5  5 2 5 3  she brings the witness  then loses the seat  yes  sakura san saw everything from start to finish   kushida called for sakura  who stood quietly behind her   sensei  sakura san is    cut off   chabashira sensei cut kushida off sharply   chabashira sensei  that s a horrible thing to say   do you mind if we participate as well  sensei   of course  it was kushida who spoke up  most likely to support sakura    she asks for a place and horikita takes it  lunch in the classroom   thanks to kushida s persuasive tears  horikita joins the strategy meeting   can we really prove sudou s innocence tomorrow  mid argument she stops listening   kushida  seated beside me as the ike yamauchi spectacle unfolded  appeared deep in thought   perhaps    murmured  then she opens her phone and says nothing more about it   ah  nothing  it s nothing  there was just something on my mind","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p163-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: she brings the witness, then loses the seat<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.163–168<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Lunch in the classroom; &quot;thanks to Kushida’s persuasive tears&quot; Horikita joins the strategy meeting. Mid-argument she stops listening: &quot;Kushida, seated beside me as the Ike/Yamauchi spectacle unfolded, appeared deep in thought.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yes. Sakura-san saw everything from start to finish.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sensei, Sakura-san is…&quot; — cut off: &quot;Chabashira-sensei cut Kushida off sharply.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Chabashira-sensei, that’s a horrible thing to say!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> &quot;Kushida called for Sakura, who stood quietly behind her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you mind if we participate as well, sensei?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> &quot;Of course, it was Kushida who spoke up, most likely to support Sakura.&quot; — she asks for a place and Horikita takes it.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Can we really prove Sudou’s innocence tomorrow?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Perhaps…&quot; — murmured, then she opens her phone and says nothing more about it.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ah, nothing. It’s nothing. There was just something on my mind.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p159-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.1: she reads Horikita better than Horikita reads herself<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.6: the idol, the persona theory, and the whisper at the door<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p179-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 5  5 6  the idol  the persona theory  and the whisper at the door that night  under kushida s orders  everyone but sudo gathers in ayanokoji s room  she asks for his computer and opens a blog   there has been progress  yes  but i ve also noticed something incredible  ayanokouji kun  can i borrow your computer for a minute   okay  have a look at this  the reveal s opening exchange is untagged   wait  is that a picture of shizuku  then  shizuku  then  she s a gravure idol  she was just featured in a young men s magazine    only the next question   do you recognize her  carries her name   do you recognize her   look closely   no  not that  this is sakura san  isn t it   sakura san  from our class   when i saw ike kun reading that weekly magazine  i remembered something  i had the feeling i d seen sakura somewhere before   but just when shizuku started to become really popular  she suddenly disappeared   i was surprised when i found out that she was an idol  but i also kind of understood it  i wonder if that s her real personality  her theory of the double life   i think that most likely  sakura san would say that her idol self is actually her false face  then  i think that she s creating another personality with makeup   i ll tell you later  right now  our priority is to resolve this case  besides  it s a personal request   i m sorry  if i told you now  it d just be a bother   if you listen to my request  ayanokouji kun i ll give you my most precious possession    whispered at the door  on tiptoe  hand on his chest  by the time the door opens the change is gone   not even the faintest trace of that frightening kushida remained  she turns the request into a transaction before she has named it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.6: the idol, the persona theory, and the whisper at the door<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.179–185<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">That night &quot;under Kushida’s orders&quot; everyone but Sudō gathers in Ayanokōji&#x27;s room; she asks for his computer and opens a blog.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;There has been progress, yes, but I’ve also noticed something incredible. Ayanokouji-kun, can I borrow your computer for a minute?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Okay. Have a look at this!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Do you recognize her?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The reveal&#x27;s opening exchange is untagged: &quot;Wait, is that a picture of Shizuku?&quot; then &quot;Shizuku?&quot; then &quot;She’s a gravure idol. She was just featured in a young men’s magazine.&quot; — only the next question, &quot;Do you recognize her?&quot;, carries her name.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Look closely.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, not that! This is Sakura-san, isn’t it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sakura-san, from our class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;When I saw Ike-kun reading that weekly magazine, I remembered something. I had the feeling I’d seen Sakura somewhere before,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But just when Shizuku started to become really popular, she suddenly disappeared.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I was surprised when I found out that she was an idol, but I also kind of understood it. I wonder if that’s her real personality?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her theory of the double life: &quot;I think that…most likely, Sakura-san would say that her idol self is actually her false face.&quot; then &quot;I think that she’s creating another personality with makeup.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’ll tell you later. Right now, our priority is to resolve this case. Besides, it’s a personal request.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m sorry. If I told you now, it’d just be a bother.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you listen to my request, Ayanokouji-kun…I’ll give you my most precious possession.&quot; — whispered at the door, on tiptoe, hand on his chest.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> By the time the door opens the change is gone: &quot;Not even the faintest trace of that frightening Kushida remained.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She turns the request into a transaction before she has named it.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p163-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: she brings the witness, then loses the seat<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p191-1\">→ After: Ch.6 open: the send-off<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p191-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 6 open  the send off her only spoken line in the chapter is the room s send off to the two people going into the hearing    do your best  horikita san  sudou kun    and horikita does not answer it  she gives the encouragement to both of them together  including the girl who has spent the volume refusing her  and the page records no reply","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 open: the send-off<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.191<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her only spoken line in the chapter is the room’s send-off to the two people going into the hearing — &quot;Do your best, Horikita-san. Sudou-kun.&quot; — and Horikita does not answer it.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She gives the encouragement to both of them together, including the girl who has spent the volume refusing her, and the page records no reply.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.6: the idol, the persona theory, and the whisper at the door<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p213-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.2: named among the people who believe Sakura<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p213-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 6  6 2  named among the people who believe sakura ayanokoji tells sakura that the belief is not his alone    horikita  kushida  and sudou do  too  all of our classmates believe you  her part is reported by him  not shown in this chapter","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p213-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.2: named among the people who believe Sakura<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.213<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Ayanokōji tells Sakura that the belief is not his alone — &quot;Horikita, Kushida, and Sudou do, too. All of our classmates believe you.&quot; Her part is reported by him, not shown in this chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p191-1\">← Before: Ch.6 open: the send-off<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p225-1\">→ After: Ch.7: her email, and the reward still to come<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p225-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 7  her email  and the reward still to come ayanokoji states that he asked her to send the email that lured the three class c students to the special building   i asked her to send an email to compel you all to come  horikita lists her hearing actions among those that  would be rewarded as well","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p225-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: her email, and the reward still to come<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.225–246<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji states that he asked her to send the email that lured the three Class C students to the special building: &quot;I asked her to send an email to compel you all to come.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita lists her hearing actions among those that &quot;would be rewarded as well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p213-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.2: named among the people who believe Sakura<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p14-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji horikita-suzune ibuki-mio sakura-airi kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 2  the first name permission  the leader nomination  and the shared meal deck of the liner  the extraordinary view  had stolen her breath away  grants ike first name permission and offers  kanjikun  in return   the exchange that sets ike s confession plan running  present when sudou fumbles horikita s first name as tomiko  the correction to suzune lands in front of the group  nominates horikita as spot leader in the circle   hirata and karuizawa  stand out too much  but responsibility is the criterion   i think that horikita san meets that criteria  ayanokoji reads the nomination as the least risk play  horikita  was so desperate to reach class a  that was crucial  walks over with a meal seat and water from her own group s ration   four people sharing three portions   while ibuki protests  are you guys stupid  you re all being way too nice  the chapter s last word on her   kushida  who wished for everyone s happiness  had charity to spare  raises her hand for river water once the vote is already tipping  which ayanokoji suspects is influence rather than conviction","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the first-name permission, the leader nomination, and the shared meal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.14–20, p.66–96<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner; the extraordinary view &quot;had stolen her breath away.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Grants Ike first-name permission and offers &quot;Kanjikun&quot; in return — the exchange that sets Ike&#x27;s confession plan running.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Present when Sudou fumbles Horikita&#x27;s first name as Tomiko; the correction to Suzune lands in front of the group.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Nominates Horikita as spot-leader in the circle — Hirata and Karuizawa &quot;stand out too much,&quot; but responsibility is the criterion: &quot;I think that Horikita-san meets that criteria.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Ayanokōji reads the nomination as the least-risk play: Horikita &quot;was so desperate to reach Class A. That was crucial.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Walks over with a meal seat and water from her own group&#x27;s ration — four people sharing three portions — while Ibuki protests &quot;Are you guys stupid? You’re all being way too nice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s last word on her: &quot;Kushida, who wished for everyone’s happiness, had charity to spare.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Raises her hand for river water once the vote is already tipping, which Ayanokōji suspects is influence rather than conviction.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.6: comforting Karuizawa<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p159-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 6  comforting karuizawa named by shinohara as one of the girls inside the tent comforting the crying karuizawa  with the victim s group from the first moment of the crisis","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: comforting Karuizawa<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.159–170<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named by Shinohara as one of the girls inside the tent comforting the crying Karuizawa.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> With the victim’s group from the first moment of the crisis.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p14-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the first-name permission, the leader nomination, and the shared meal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p171-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: chasing Sakura<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p171-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 6  6 1  chasing sakura chases sakura into the forest after karuizawa s teasing drives her off  goes after her alone  judging it dangerous for someone to enter the woods by herself","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p171-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: chasing Sakura<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.171–178<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chases Sakura into the forest after Karuizawa’s teasing drives her off.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Goes after her alone, judging it dangerous for someone to enter the woods by herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p159-1\">← Before: Ch.6: comforting Karuizawa<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p192-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.4: the smile question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p192-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 6  6 4  the smile question left behind with horikita s group  she whispers why   and spends the walk trying to draw horikita out   why were you left behind  what about your usual group of friends   ah  yeah  well  it s   well  to tell you the truth  mii chan is having her time of the month  she always feels awful when it happens  so her other friends are with her in the tent  the nickname  mii chan  has no published name form on this page  the girl is left unidentified  chose this group to talk to her  horikita grills her for it and dislikes her openly   i wanted to talk to you  horikita san  and thought this was a good chance  you know  we haven t really talked at all during this trip  have we  well  as soon as it gets dark out  let s head to bed   you re so mean  horikita san  even though your face is so cute when you re sleeping  the narration notes a hidden side   a dramatic change from her usual persona  to the point where she could calmly abuse other people  the everyday kushida is fundamentally kind  cheerful  and cute  and loves to help others   ayanokouji kun and horikita san have been on pretty good terms from the beginning  right  i was trying to think of what the reason might be   ah  i think i might have found something that ayanokouji kun and horikita san have in common   well  look at them closely  yamauchi kun  notice anything   ha ha  s sorry  yamauchi kun  i started trouble  are you okay   well  don t you know  i hardly see the two of them laugh  that s it  it s like  i don t think i ve ever seen ayanokouji kun or horikita san smile  points out that she has never seen him or horikita smile   i ve seen you with a bitter smile  sure  but never a genuine grin  something from the bottom of your heart  i ve never seen you laugh so hard you had to clutch your stomach  ayanokouji kun  or perhaps you ve just   never shown that side of yourself to me   how about we practice smiling just once  what do you think  the translation leaves the offer untagged  placed here against her preceding lines about smiling  the last one left  she pairs off with ibuki for the search   i m looking forward to working with you  ibuki san","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p192-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.4: the smile question<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.192–199<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Left behind with Horikita’s group, she whispers why — and spends the walk trying to draw Horikita out.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Why were you left behind? What about your usual group of friends?”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ah, yeah. Well, it’s…”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, to tell you the truth, Mii-chan is having her time of the month. She always feels awful when it happens. So her other friends are with her in the tent.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The nickname “Mii-chan” has no published name form on this page; the girl is left unidentified.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Chose this group to talk to her; Horikita grills her for it and dislikes her openly.<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wanted to talk to you, Horikita-san, and thought this was a good chance. You know, we haven’t really talked at all during this trip, have we? Well, as soon as it gets dark out, let’s head to bed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re so mean, Horikita-san. Even though your face is so cute when you’re sleeping.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narration notes a hidden side — a dramatic change from her usual persona, to the point where she could calmly abuse other people.<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The everyday Kushida is fundamentally kind, cheerful, and cute, and loves to help others.<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun and Horikita-san have been on pretty good terms from the beginning, right? I was trying to think of what the reason might be.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah. I think I might have found something that Ayanokouji-kun and Horikita-san have in common,”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, look at them closely, Yamauchi-kun. Notice anything?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ha ha… S-sorry, Yamauchi-kun. I started trouble. Are you okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, don’t you know? I hardly see the two of them laugh! That’s it. It’s like, I don’t think I’ve ever seen Ayanokouji-kun or Horikita-san smile.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Points out that she has never seen him or Horikita smile.<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve seen you with a bitter smile, sure, but never a genuine grin, something from the bottom of your heart. I’ve never seen you laugh so hard you had to clutch your stomach, Ayanokouji-kun. Or perhaps you’ve just … never shown that side of yourself to me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How about we practice smiling just once? What do you think?”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The translation leaves the offer untagged; placed here against her preceding lines about smiling.<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> The last one left, she pairs off with Ibuki for the search.<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m looking forward to working with you, Ibuki-san!”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p171-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: chasing Sakura<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p200-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.5: witness and swimmer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p200-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 6  6 5  witness and swimmer watches yamauchi s strange approach to horikita with ibuki  quizzical  and sees the mud go on before anyone reacts  with ibuki  one of the two who notices yamauchi s behavior in time to wonder at it  goes down to the river in her swimsuit with horikita while the shower line waits  the pair appear in swimsuits together   horikita to wash the mud off  her along for the swim  the river invitation that follows    i think i m going to go for a swim  ibuki san  do you want to go for a swim with me    is untagged and is left as a chapter attribution gap","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p200-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.5: witness and swimmer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.200–202<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches Yamauchi’s strange approach to Horikita with Ibuki, quizzical, and sees the mud go on before anyone reacts.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">With Ibuki, one of the two who notices Yamauchi’s behavior in time to wonder at it.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q action\">Goes down to the river in her swimsuit with Horikita while the shower line waits.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The pair appear in swimsuits together — Horikita to wash the mud off, her along for the swim.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The river invitation that follows — “I think I’m going to go for a swim. Ibuki-san, do you want to go for a swim with me?” — is untagged and is left as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p192-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.4: the smile question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p15-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 2  one of the three  and the old push named in the first semester recollection of the only people ayanokoji could talk to  listed with horikita and sakura as the three he talked with   his school life hadn t been all that bad  her push for friendship with horikita in the cafe during the first semester is cited as proof that pushing would only make her distance herself further","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p15-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: one of the three, and the old push<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.15, p.18<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the first-semester recollection of the only people Ayanokōji could talk to.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Listed with Horikita and Sakura as the three he talked with — his school life hadn’t been all that bad.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her push for friendship with Horikita in the café during the first semester is cited as proof that pushing would only make her distance herself further.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p27-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2: the hallway interrupt and the message compare<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p27-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 2  2 2  the hallway interrupt and the message compare exits a second deck room into the hallway mid meeting plan  interrupts sakura s appeal  then compares school messages with ayanokoji   huh  ayanokouji kun and sakura san  what are you doing here   ah  did i interrupt  i didn t mean to  i was supposed to meet up with some friends   i ve made plans to go see some girls from class c today  do you want to come  ayanokouji kun   oh jeez  come on  you surprised me a little  ayanokouji kun  you re funny  her true self  seemed puzzled by my response  when he says yes   the mask slips a little before the smooth recovery  without hesitation shows him her message  20 40  a room two doors from his  draws nearer  curious about his chat with horikita  the bright entrance that sends sakura fleeing  kushida apologises to no evident purpose  invites  reads his joke  shares her phone  watches his screen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.2: the hallway interrupt and the message compare<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.27–31<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Exits a second-deck room into the hallway mid-meeting-plan; interrupts Sakura’s appeal, then compares school messages with Ayanokōji.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Huh? Ayanokouji-kun and Sakura-san? What are you doing here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ah, did I interrupt? I didn’t mean to. I was supposed to meet up with some friends.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ve made plans to go see some girls from Class C today. Do you want to come, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh jeez, come on. You surprised me a little. Ayanokouji-kun, you’re funny.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her true self “seemed puzzled by my response” when he says yes — the mask slips a little before the smooth recovery.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Without hesitation shows him her message: 20:40, a room two doors from his.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Draws nearer, curious about his chat with Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> The bright entrance that sends Sakura fleeing; Kushida apologises to no evident purpose.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Invites, reads his joke, shares her phone, watches his screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p15-1\">← Before: Ch.2: one of the three, and the old push<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5: the puzzled arrival<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 2  2 5  the puzzled arrival wanders into the 20 40 gathering without understanding the group structure  then reads the room fast enough to keep up   huh  hirata kun  oh  ayanokouji kun  too  what are you all doing here   hmm  group  i don t understand  i did get an email telling me to come here at this time  wow  there really are some amazing people here  huh  somewhat taken back yet respectful of everyone gathered  by fragments of conversation she begins to grasp the situation   um  well  so  it feels like a lot of really difficult things are about to come our way   ah ha  don t worry  it s okay  like hirata kun said  all i can do is my best  oh  i haven t really had many chances to talk with katsuragi kun and ryuuen kun yet  i d like to get along with you all  too   speaking to everyone present  delivers the last line without anxiety  disgust  displeasure  or joy in her voice  takes his composure as her anchor  names him as someone she hasn t talked to yet  names him the same way  in the same breath  present for her cold exit","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.5: the puzzled arrival<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.60–61<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Wanders into the 20:40 gathering without understanding the group structure, then reads the room fast enough to keep up.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Huh, Hirata-kun? Oh, Ayanokouji-kun, too? What are you all doing here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hmm? Group? I don’t understand. I did get an email telling me to come here at this time… Wow, there really are some amazing people here, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Um, well. So, it feels like a lot of really difficult things are about to come our way,”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Somewhat taken back yet respectful of everyone gathered; by fragments of conversation she begins to grasp the situation.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah ha! Don’t worry, it’s okay! Like Hirata-kun said, all I can do is my best. Oh, I haven’t really had many chances to talk with Katsuragi-kun and Ryuuen-kun yet. I’d like to get along with you all, too.” (speaking to everyone present)<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Delivers the last line without anxiety, disgust, displeasure, or joy in her voice.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Takes his composure as her anchor.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Names him as someone she hasn’t talked to yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Names him the same way, in the same breath.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Present for her cold exit.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p27-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the hallway interrupt and the message compare<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p64-1\">→ After: Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p64-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 3  named on the dragon roster one roster line in horikita s hand   class d s other two dragon members with her  listed with hirata yousuke as the class d pair  ayanokoji calls them  both excellent students  and representatives of our class  and the strongest hand class d could deal  dragon groupmate on the biased list  dragon groupmate on the same line","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p64-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.64<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One roster line in Horikita’s hand — Class D’s other two Dragon members with her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Listed with Hirata Yousuke as the Class D pair; Ayanokōji calls them “both excellent students, and representatives of our class” and the strongest hand Class D could deal.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Dragon groupmate on the biased list.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Dragon groupmate on the same line.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p60-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the puzzled arrival<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p77-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the check on Horikita and the popularity bar<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p77-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 3  the check on horikita and the popularity bar named as one of the two who might keep horikita in check  despite powerful foes  horikita was indomitable   hirata and kushida would hopefully keep her in check  in the talent comparison  even hirata and kushida might find themselves outmatched  despite their overabundance of friends  kushida was always kushida   and karuizawa probably rivaled kushida in terms of popularity","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p77-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the check on Horikita and the popularity bar<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.77, p.84, p.109<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as one of the two who might keep Horikita in check.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Despite powerful foes, Horikita was indomitable — Hirata and Kushida would hopefully keep her in check.<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> In the talent comparison, even Hirata and Kushida might find themselves outmatched, despite their overabundance of friends.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kushida was always Kushida — and Karuizawa probably rivaled Kushida in terms of popularity.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p64-1\">← Before: Ch.3: named on the Dragon roster<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p113-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.5–§3.6: the VIP name and the starlit hug<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p113-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 3  3 5 3 6  the vip name and the starlit hug named dragon vip on hirata s erased screen  four pages later alone on the night deck among the couples  she hugs ayanokoji and flees   dragon group  kushida san    the vip position in the extremely well stacked dragon group is an enormous advantage and terrifying   once they knew her identity  she was at their mercy  hirata s reassurance rides on the three class d dragon members being  the best we had to offer    they would not reveal her   huh  oh  ayanokouji kun   yeah  i am  i just couldn t seem to sleep   i m fine  what about you  ayanokouji kun  are you all alone   so we re both alone  i admit  i felt a little ashamed being alone  this makes me feel better   you re already leaving   i see  well  i ll see you tomorrow  good night  ayanokouji kun  unexpectedly wraps her arms around his chest    even in this cold  i felt the warmth of her body through her jersey   i m sorry  i i just felt so lonely  i think  she whispered   small voice after the   pause  the words hit him  like a fighter smacking me right in the jaw   s sorry  i  um i just hugged you so suddenly  ayanokouji kun  good night  she stammered   then quickly scurries away  might be blushing in the dark  jersey after a bath  complimentary shampoo scent that somehow is not that scent  alone among couples  the narrator s chest tightens imagining a boyfriend  the night deck encounter and the hug neither of them can explain","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p113-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.5–§3.6: the VIP name and the starlit hug<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.113, p.117–121<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named Dragon VIP on Hirata’s erased screen; four pages later alone on the night deck among the couples, she hugs Ayanokōji and flees.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Huh? Oh, Ayanokouji…kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yeah, I am. I just couldn’t seem to sleep.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m fine. What about you, Ayanokouji-kun? Are you all alone?”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> “Dragon Group, Kushida-san.” — the VIP position in the extremely well-stacked Dragon group is an enormous advantage and terrifying: “Once they knew her identity, she was at their mercy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Hirata’s reassurance rides on the three Class D Dragon members being “the best we had to offer” — they would not reveal her.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So we’re both alone? I admit, I felt a little ashamed being alone. This makes me feel better.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re already leaving?”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Well, I’ll see you tomorrow. Good night, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Unexpectedly wraps her arms around his chest — “Even in this cold, I felt the warmth of her body through her jersey.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry. I…I just felt so lonely, I think,” she whispered. (small voice after the “…” pause; the words hit him “like a fighter smacking me right in the jaw”)<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “S-sorry. I, um…I just hugged you so suddenly, Ayanokouji-kun. Good night!” she stammered. (then quickly scurries away; might be blushing in the dark)<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Jersey after a bath, complimentary-shampoo scent that somehow is not that scent; alone among couples; the narrator’s chest tightens imagining a boyfriend.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The night-deck encounter and the hug neither of them can explain.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–121<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p77-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the check on Horikita and the popularity bar<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the ringleaders<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p116-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 3  the ringleaders named as one of the two ringleaders ayanokoji considers using  the ringleaders were hirata and kushida   using them is muttered as impossible with three days left","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the ringleaders<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.116<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as one of the two ringleaders Ayanokōji considers using.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The ringleaders were Hirata and Kushida — using them is muttered as impossible with three days left.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p113-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.5–§3.6: the VIP name and the starlit hug<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p127-1\">→ After: Ch.4: outer and inner, then the star player<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p127-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 4  outer and inner  then the star player named as an example of the gap between a person s outer and inner selves  innermost thoughts aren t immediately apparent   take kushida  ibuki  or even me  with horikita and hirata  she is called a star player in the class d line up","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p127-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: outer and inner, then the star player<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.127, p.140<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as an example of the gap between a person’s outer and inner selves.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Innermost thoughts aren’t immediately apparent — take Kushida, Ibuki, or even me.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> With Horikita and Hirata, she is called a star player in the Class D line-up.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the ringleaders<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p144-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: the invitation inside<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p144-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 4  4 1  the invitation inside spots ayanokoji and ichinose in the dragon corridor  waves them into the three way  then exits when ryuuen leaves with  my friends are calling me   huh  ayanokouji kun  what are you doing here  are you waiting for horikita san  asked kushida   oh  ichinose san  hello  now  this is odd  well  i should say i didn t expect to see the two of you together  said kushida  surprised ayanokoji and class b s leader know each other   she didn t know  he stiffens at her approach  remembering yesterday s scene  she has gone back to her usual self as though nothing changed   oh  those two  they re still discussing things with ryuuen kun right now  maybe you could step inside  kushida gestured toward the door  as if inviting us in   oh  i think it s fine  besides  the test period is only one hour  any time after that  we re free to come and go as we please  besides  they may not be talking about the test   ah  i should be going  my friends are calling me  said kushida  the ryuuen conversation she reports is the reason she opens the door    they may not be talking about the test  named in the corridor as the person ayanokoji is waiting for  the excuse ichinose accepts","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p144-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.1: the invitation inside<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.144–149<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Spots Ayanokōji and Ichinose in the Dragon corridor, waves them into the three-way, then exits when Ryuuen leaves with “My friends are calling me.”<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Huh? Ayanokouji-kun, what are you doing here? Are you waiting for Horikita-san?” asked Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh! Ichinose-san! Hello. Now, this is odd. Well, I should say I didn’t expect to see the two of you together,” said Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh, those two. They’re still discussing things with Ryuuen-kun right now. Maybe you could step inside?” Kushida gestured toward the door, as if inviting us in.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Surprised Ayanokōji and Class B’s leader know each other — she didn’t know.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He stiffens at her approach, remembering yesterday’s scene; she has gone back to her usual self as though nothing changed.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, I think it’s fine. Besides, the test period is only one hour. Any time after that, we’re free to come and go as we please. Besides, they may not be talking about the test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, I should be going. My friends are calling me,” said Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The Ryuuen conversation she reports is the reason she opens the door — “they may not be talking about the test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Named in the corridor as the person Ayanokōji is waiting for; the excuse Ichinose accepts.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p127-1\">← Before: Ch.4: outer and inner, then the star player<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p185-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.5: the fallback contact<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p185-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 4  4 5  the fallback contact named once as the risk ayanokoji avoids   if hirata had not had manabe s info  he would have had to ask her for it  the cross class contact info hirata supplies saves the kushida detour  no scene presence  one line of planning in ayanokoji s narration","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p185-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.5: the fallback contact<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.185<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as the risk Ayanokōji avoids — if Hirata had not had Manabe’s info, he would have had to ask her for it.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The cross-class contact info Hirata supplies saves the Kushida detour.<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence; one line of planning in Ayanokōji’s narration.<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p144-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: the invitation inside<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p207-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.1–5.2: the Dragon VIP behind the swap<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p207-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 5  5 1 5 2  the dragon vip behind the swap named as the dragon group s vip from hirata s tip   the name ayanokoji s phone swap trap runs on  never spoken in the room  the source of the identification   i d already heard from hirata that kushida was the dragon group s vip  the swap pairs her phone with kushida s so a traitor submitting horikita fails  the hidden mechanism of outcome  1   she never appears on screen in this half  no scene presence  the row records the fact the plan depends on","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p207-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.1–5.2: the Dragon VIP behind the swap<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.207, 217<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the Dragon group’s VIP from Hirata’s tip — the name Ayanokōji’s phone-swap trap runs on, never spoken in the room.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The source of the identification; “I’d already heard from Hirata that Kushida was the Dragon group’s VIP.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The swap pairs her phone with Kushida’s so a traitor submitting Horikita fails.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The hidden mechanism of Outcome #1 — she never appears on screen in this half.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence; the row records the fact the plan depends on.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p185-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.5: the fallback contact<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p239-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.3: the name that broke the table<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p239-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 5  5 3  the name that broke the table named aloud as dragon group vip by ryuuen   known to him since day two   and the fact that dragon cleared outcome  1 without a traitor makes her the centre of ayanokoji s 1  explanation  he never turned traitor despite knowing  the reveal is saved for the cafe audience   kushida kikyou   his line  naming her  her confidence    no one in the dragon group has turned traitor    is exactly what he weaponises  flabbergasted beside her  he had carefully protected her identity all test  the seed planted theory  tell everyone  kushida is the vip  in the riskless half hour and even katsuragi votes for the 1  dragon  outcome  1   the entire group answered correctly at the end of the test  she is not at the cafe  the row records the public naming of her vip status","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p239-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.3: the name that broke the table<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.239–242<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named aloud as Dragon group VIP by Ryuuen — known to him since day two — and the fact that Dragon cleared Outcome #1 without a traitor makes her the centre of Ayanokōji’s 1% explanation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Kushida Kikyou.” (his line, naming her)<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> He never turned traitor despite knowing; the reveal is saved for the café audience.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her confidence — “no one in the Dragon group has turned traitor” — is exactly what he weaponises.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Flabbergasted beside her; he had carefully protected her identity all test.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The seed-planted theory: tell everyone “Kushida is the VIP” in the riskless half hour and even Katsuragi votes for the 1%.<span class=\"pg\">p.241-242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Dragon: Outcome #1 — the entire group answered correctly at the end of the test.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She is not at the café; the row records the public naming of her VIP status.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4-p207-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.1–5.2: the Dragon VIP behind the swap<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p28-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 2  a passing mention in the partner list named once as the girl he skips  he expects horikita to decline and lacks the courage to ask kushida  the refusal is his  not hers   i didn t have the courage to invite kushida","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p28-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: a passing mention in the partner list<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.28<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as the girl he skips: he expects Horikita to decline and lacks the courage to ask Kushida.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The refusal is his, not hers: “I didn’t have the courage to invite Kushida.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p41-1\">→ After: Ch.2: a passing mention in the rescue call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p41-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 2  a passing mention in the rescue call named once as someone unsuited to fetching help for the trapped pair  ruled out with karuizawa on the same line   kushida and karuizawa were probably likewise unsuited to the task","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p41-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: a passing mention in the rescue call<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.41<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named once as someone unsuited to fetching help for the trapped pair.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ruled out with Karuizawa on the same line: “Kushida and Karuizawa were probably likewise unsuited to the task.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p28-1\">← Before: Ch.2: a passing mention in the partner list<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p49-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the invitation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p49-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"inogashira-kokoro kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 3  the invitation kushida opens the chapter with a group chat invite to celebrate inogashira s birthday and help her make friends   next wednesday is inogashira san s birthday  she reaches out to the quiet  plain girl who has few friends","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p49-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the invitation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.49<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida opens the chapter with a group-chat invite to celebrate Inogashira&#x27;s birthday and help her make friends.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"index.html#inogashira-kokoro\">Inogashira Kokoro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Next Wednesday is Inogashira-san’s birthday.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Inogashira Kokoro<\/b> She reaches out to the quiet, plain girl who has few friends.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p41-1\">← Before: Ch.2: a passing mention in the rescue call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p60-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the birthday list and the boundaries<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p60-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei ike-kanji horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 3  the birthday list and the boundaries kushida arrives at ak s room with her memorized birthday list and works the august 29 question   i think i ve memorized the birthdates of everyone who s told me  more or less   if it s a first year girl  i should know everyone  but i can t think of anyone who fits  she defends him  the hair loss came from illness in childhood  ike is made to cut it out   katsuragi kun lost his hair completely when he was young  due to illness   okay  so  from now on  you ll address him properly  won t you  she steers ike toward apologizing to shinohara with one gentle question   you understand what you should do about it  right  she produces horikita s birthday from memory   surprising ak given their mutual hatred   it s on february 15  ak notes he is one of the few who knows kushida and horikita hate each other  curious about the gift but firm  interference is off the table   kanji kun  you can t interfere   of course i m curious  but getting in the way is not okay  she has his contact from the ship test group and offers it  ak declines a cold call   i have katsuragi kun s contact information   i asked him for it  kushida leaves the investigation on ak s desk with ike s and sudou s pressure behind it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p60-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the birthday list and the boundaries<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.60–66<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida arrives at AK&#x27;s room with her memorized birthday list and works the August 29 question.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I think I’ve memorized the birthdates of everyone who’s told me, more or less.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If it’s a first-year girl, I should know everyone, but I can’t think of anyone who fits”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Katsuragi-kun lost his hair completely when he was young, due to illness.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> She defends him: the hair loss came from illness in childhood; Ike is made to cut it out.<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, so, from now on, you’ll address him properly, won’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> She steers Ike toward apologizing to Shinohara with one gentle question.<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You understand what you should do about it, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She produces Horikita&#x27;s birthday from memory — surprising AK given their mutual hatred.<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s on February 15.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> AK notes he is one of the few who knows Kushida and Horikita hate each other.<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Curious about the gift but firm: interference is off the table.<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kanji-kun, you can’t interfere,”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I’m curious, but getting in the way is not okay.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> She has his contact from the ship-test group and offers it; AK declines a cold call.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have Katsuragi-kun’s contact information.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I asked him for it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Kushida leaves the investigation on AK&#x27;s desk with Ike&#x27;s and Sudou&#x27;s pressure behind it.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p49-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the invitation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p83-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the girl on the celebration team<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p83-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji katsuragi-kouhei kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 3  the girl on the celebration team kushida joins the next day s run after ike tells her  she greets ak and questions his uniform   hello  ayanokouji kun  ike told her about the katsuragi present  she said she definitely wanted to help   i ll help out with the present s cost  of course  she fronts the ambush   after the ship test he is most familiar with her   and cracks his guard   sorry for bothering you  katsuragi kun  do you have a moment   isn t it your birthday today  katsuragi kun   do you have plans today  her smile is read as smitten inducing  even class a s leader is not an easy target  the cake they ambush with is the one she chose","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p83-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the girl on the celebration team<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.83, 88<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida joins the next day&#x27;s run after Ike tells her; she greets AK and questions his uniform.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hello, Ayanokouji-kun,”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll help out with the present’s cost, of course,”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Sorry for bothering you, Katsuragi-kun. Do you have a moment?”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Ike told her about the Katsuragi present; she said she definitely wanted to help.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> She fronts the ambush — after the ship test he is most familiar with her — and cracks his guard.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t it your birthday today, Katsuragi-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you have plans today?”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Her smile is read as smitten-inducing; even Class A&#x27;s leader is not an easy target.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> The cake they ambush with is the one she chose.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v4_5-p60-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the birthday list and the boundaries<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
